/-!
# OSLF FULL Status Tracker

Machine-readable tracker for what is already formalized versus what is still
missing for a full presheaf-topos/native-type-theory OSLF lift.

This module is intentionally concrete: every entry includes a code reference
string so status reports can link back to Lean artifacts directly.

Two integration results refine, but do not close, the remaining source-level
obligations. `MultiRewriteSchematic.singleton_step_iff` identifies singleton
document steps with canonical premise-aware, equation-modulo steps when the
added library has no unary declarations. Its retained join witnesses preserve
shared bindings and ordered windows; general equation search is not an algorithm
provided by that theorem. `WMCalculusEvidenceConversion.conversion_iff_allReadings`
proves completeness of explicitly generated evidence conversion for closed WM
terms. It does not make the original directed calculus complete, and
`pendingExtractions_does_not_descend` proves that the conversion quotient forgets
pending computational work. Neither result supplies the n-ary classifying theory
or the remaining native dependent source theorems.

`WMCalculusBindingSignature` derives all four intrinsic operator arities from
that same authored signature. Its observation term is both a multisorted clone
operation and a morphism to the singleton evidence context; precomposition is
the existing simultaneous substitution. Erasure preserves the actual directed
extraction computation under any sort-preserving substitution. This establishes
the finite-arity syntactic action, not a dependent classifying universal property
or soundness of arbitrary raw authored equation instances. A two-variable
control proves that erasure changes under context substitution, so this
intrinsic presheaf cannot be identified with the constant raw-pattern program
presheaf without an explicit comparison map.

`SyntacticTermPresheaf` packages intrinsic terms as a genuine presheaf on
contexts and simultaneous substitutions, naturally isomorphic to Yoneda at
the one-variable context of each sort. `WMCalculusIntrinsicPresheafObservation`
makes all four authored core constructors natural maps on these presheaves:
`Revise`, `Extract`, `Combine`, and nullary `EvidenceZero`. The authored
extraction redex and contractum are natural
maps on two states and a shared query; their pointwise rewrite and its
reindexing by every sorted substitution are proved. This map supplies the
native presheaf predicate fibration's dependent context, so the indexed Σ/Π
introduction and elimination laws apply
to observation predicates. A negative theorem rules out treating objectwise
erasure as a map to the constant raw-pattern presheaf. This supplies a
context-indexed observation seam, not a complete classifying λ-theory.

The guarded overlap/scope vertex now has its own declaration-derived binding
signature. A structural morphism embeds the directed core and transports
typed terms, substitution, and canonical equation-modulo steps into that
vertex. All four added constructors act naturally on intrinsic term
presheaves. Overlap extraction and forgetting idempotence compute at every
context and after reindexing; outside-scope forgetting still requires an
explicit relation answer, and the empty provider supplies none. The separate
structural-equation core has no literal structural morphism into this
equation-free vertex, so this is not yet a combined structural quotient or a
semantic compatibility theorem for arbitrary overlap/forgetting models.

A separate validated structural combined presentation now retains the same
typed overlap/scope grammar and guarded computations while making the three
evidence monoid laws authored equations. The structural WM core embeds in it
by an equation- and rewrite-preserving morphism, so its directed steps have a
forward simulation. The source's premise-free equation instances, contextual
equivalence, and equation-saturated OSLF steps also transport forward. This
does not identify it with the equation-free directed vertex or interpret correlated
overlap and forgetting in every lawful reading.

A concrete counting reading shows the combined root laws are consistent in a
non-additive case: ordinary revision adds counts, overlap-aware merge takes
their maximum, and a nonzero overlap factor corrects duplicates. Scoped
forgetting is idempotent and preserves observations outside its scope. The
eight authored constructors now have a semantic interpretation on a certified
fragment of the existing intrinsic terms. That interpretation commutes with
supported simultaneous substitutions, and model environments reindex with
identity and composition laws. Its evidence-answer fibre follows that action.
Core extraction, the three evidence equations,
overlap extraction, and forgetting are sound under their exact laws. A typed
counting canary separates overlap merge from revision. The generic lambda
operator is outside the interpreted fragment. A separately checked scope
provider now connects accepted premise answers to the semantic outside-scope
condition; arbitrary relation providers do not inherit that certificate.
This is not a model of every generated binder form or a proof of full guarded
subject reduction.

The counting model also satisfies the five nontrivial behavioral congruence
obligations for the added constructors. Neither interpretation handles
arbitrary raw authored patterns yet.

The two combined presentations have identical authored constructor lists,
so a generic same-terms binding-signature map transports intrinsic terms and
substitution between them without changing their context lists. Its forward
and reverse maps compose to the identity on intrinsic terms as well as on
signature morphisms, including generic binder representation forms. This
transport also preserves raw erasure exactly. The
presentations are not operationally identical: evidence commutation is a
directed rewrite only in the equation-free vertex. The model fold over the
directed vertex transports into a supported relational interpretation of the
structural presentation. On the authored first-order fragment, equal erasures
give equal values for arbitrary certificates, so the structural relation is
functional wherever its support certificate exists. The three structural
evidence equations consequently preserve and reflect every denotation of
supported terms. For a supported source term and supported substitution,
denotation after substitution is equivalent at each value to denotation under
the reindexed environment. A certified structural evidence term denotes an
answer exactly when the existing dependent evidence fibre contains that
answer; the result is independent of certificate choice. Two supported
intrinsic presentations with the same raw erasure have exactly the same model
answers. An evidence-sorted
generic substitution term remains unsupported even in the concrete counting
reading, whose evidence carrier is inhabited. This does not reflect support
for arbitrary generic binder/collection forms or prove all raw equation
instances sound
under arbitrary contexts.

On the certified first-order fragment, an explicit assignment of schema names
to intrinsic context variables now gives a named raw pattern. Applying the
actual MeTTaIL binding list to that pattern is exactly raw erasure after
intrinsic simultaneous substitution when each variable binding matches its
assigned image. The actual matcher accepts repeated evidence names with
consistent images and rejects conflicting images. On the combined vertex's
checked first-order open fragment, used-name resolution now also yields an
intrinsic supported receipt and removes the hand-supplied source certificate
from both matcher directions. Target captures still need their own support
receipts. A generic declaration-derived open codec now computes an intrinsically
sorted term for every typed, first-order-compilable source pattern and computes
intrinsic constructor-tree substitution images for accepted checked answers.
The existing supported WM fragment's named erasure agrees with that generic
renderer. A generic proof-relevant ordinary-constructor certificate specializes
to the existing combined-WM `FirstOrder` support on all eight authored forms.
Consequently the actual checked matcher computes both source and image terms
with semantic support, and that computed pair satisfies the existing
denotational substitution law. At Evidence sort, the same computed result
now yields an equivalence, for every answer and target environment, between
Prime's semantic dependent answer family at the target and the source family
pulled back along the computed substitution. These Type-valued fibres are
subsingleton correctness receipts. Supported substitutions form a Mathlib
wide subcategory of the existing context category; model environments form
a certificate-independent functor, and answer transport has identity and
composition coherence. Computing the source and substitution no longer
requires an inhabited model environment. Checked Extract admission also
composes with a decoded outside-scope guard, an actual finite-fuel engine
occurrence, and a dependent consumer in the existing semantic families CwF.
The occurrence retains the local rule/alternative indices, not a stable
cross-version identity or the recursive premise derivation.
This remains the first-order compiler fragment:
it does not interpret generic binders or collections, or prove that every
sorted authored equation instance has an interpretation certificate.

`WMCalculusStructuralPresentation` authors evidence commutativity,
associativity, and right identity as equations over the same sorted WM
signature, while extraction through revision remains a directed computation.
The three equations are sorted as schemas and their typed generators are
sound in every lawful reading. Every typed evidence equality that holds in
all lawful readings can be replayed by the authored equations and directed
extraction rule after taking conversion closure. The generic raw equation
matcher can still instantiate an evidence variable with an ill-sorted state
pattern. `OpenSortedEquationInstance` supplies context-indexed schema
substitutions, and all three typed structural generators instantiate it;
named evidence demonstrates why its closed predecessor is insufficient.
The existing typed occurrence zipper now proves replacement under an
explicit representation-shape condition. Its WM specialization proves that
each structural law preserves typing through any already typed syntactic
occurrence, while the authored equation theory relates the same endpoints.
The same replacement also preserves binder metadata, object form and scope,
placing each certified WM equation edge inside the existing native typed
open-pattern equation setoid, including contexts that cross binders.
The complete generated evidence conversion preserves free-atom sorting in
both directions and therefore transports native open-pattern admission across
all lawful WM readings, provided its source was admitted. Reflexive semantic
agreement alone cannot type a State/Query name clash.
Generated evidence conversion also replays through actual authored equation
and computation edges with typed WM evidence at every intermediate vertex.
Thus equality in every lawful reading yields a path in the native open-pattern
carrier; the reverse implication for arbitrary authored paths is not proved.
For the equation-free minimal vertex, operational adequacy proves that every
contextual reduct of an admitted WM encoding remains in that complete native
carrier. In the structural presentation, authored extraction has admitted
source and target and remains directed; this does not grant arbitrary raw
equation intermediates typed operational soundness.
A State-for-evidence instance proves that the raw authored equation generator
is not stable on every open typed fiber, so the generic whole-fiber lifting
theorem cannot establish the converse. The converse for a disciplined typed
equational conversion remains outstanding.
-/

