namespace Mettapedia.OSLF.Framework.FULLStatus

/-- Current completion state for a FULL-OSLF milestone. -/
inductive MilestoneStatus where
  | done
  | inProgress
  | missing
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- One traceability row in the FULL-OSLF tracker. -/
structure Milestone where
  area : String
  title : String
  status : MilestoneStatus
  codeRef : String
  note : String
  deriving Repr

/-- Central FULL-OSLF status table.

    `status = done` means the artifact is formalized in Lean.
    `status = inProgress` means interface/hook exists but full theorem is pending.
    `status = missing` means no complete implementation/theorem yet. -/
def tracker : List Milestone :=
  [ { area := "Scopes and Fixpoints"
      title := "Least fixpoints over the predicate frame, generated scopes, and a shape as a formula"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/FormulaFixpoint.lean: lfp / lfp_unfold / lfp_le / orWith / andWith / diaOf; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedScope.lean: scopeStep / generatedScope / scope_induction / sizeOf_quote_lt_left / inScope / inScope_iff; Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/Recursive.lean: BranchShape / BranchShape.Matches / BranchDescription / Signature.declared / Satisfies.headed / Satisfies.collected / satisfies_iff_layer / Satisfies.least / CollectionBranch.signature / CollectionBranch.pairTerm_satisfies / CollectionBranch.apply_not_satisfies; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedScopeSignature.lean: language / State / Branch / describe / signature / quotable_atomA / quotable_par / inScope_quote / inScope_composite / inScope_nested / not_quotable_atomC / not_inScope_atomC / atomADecide / atomAName / bridge / bridge_closed / quotable_of_inScope_quote / satisfies_inScope_of_generatedScope / inScope_iff_generatedScope / quotable_iff_generatedScope / inScope_iff_descent / descent_composite / descent_atomC; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/TubeShape.lean: reachStep / reachStep_apply / Reaches / reaches_induction / IsTube / reachFormula / reachFormula_size / stationSem / sem_reachFormula_iff / isTube_iff_sem / formula_separates / tube_separates; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedScopeRho.lean: quote / drop / par / quote_par_injective / no_selfCode_left / no_selfCode_right / sizeOf_drop_lt_left / sizeOf_drop_lt_right / PartAdmitted / scopeStep / generatedScope / mem_of_parts / mem_of_atoms / mem_of_drop_left / scope_induction / inScope / generatedScope_of_inScope / AtomsAvoidDrops / not_drop_of_atom / inScope_of_generatedScope / inScope_iff / Specimen.isNil_disjoint / Specimen.base_in_scope / Specimen.drop_in_scope / Specimen.nil_not_in_scope / Specimen.other_not_in_scope / Specimen.specimen_agrees"
      note := "Predicates form a complete lattice, so monotone transformers have least fixed points by Knaster-Tarski; the connectives supply monotone transformers, so generators built from them have them too. A generated scope is such a fixed point, and its membership is decided by descent: the split is unique and quoting a part is strictly smaller than quoting the whole, which is the no-self-code property in the form the termination measure needs. Procedure and fixed point are proved to agree in both directions. The name scope of rho is now built with the drop coercion the source's generator recurses through, so the generator written is the source's: a name is the quote of a composition each of whose parts is an atom or the drop of a name already in the scope. The two hypotheses that construction is supposed to need are discharged rather than assumed. Disjointness -- that the decomposition is unique -- is the injectivity of the quote of a composition, proved. No-self-code is proved by the size argument for representatives: a name cannot be the quote of a composition that drops it, because such a term would contain itself properly, and that is what makes the descent terminate with no side condition. Where the property stops being free is stated and not crossed: modulo rho's equations it is not a size argument, since the quote of a drop collapses, and the equational form is not claimed. A second disjointness condition is load-bearing and is named: the descent reads a part as a drop when it is one, so an atom that also accepts a drop makes the procedure incomplete; under atoms that avoid drops the procedure and the fixed point agree in both directions, with positive instances through the coercion and negatives outside it. The tube shape is stated as a formula over a pipe network - a directed pathway from intake to expulsion and no pathway back - with the negative half proved by the fixed point's own induction principle, and two networks differing by one return pipe separated by it. That question is now settled the other way, in the row below: the formula language carries the binder and this layer keeps only Knaster-Tarski itself. The structural layer's recursive signature now admits collection branches beside headed ones: a branch says what it matches at the root, either a named constructor or a collection of a declared kind, and a collection branch is witnessed by the presentation declaring a carrier of that kind exactly as a headed branch is witnessed by a declared rule. A bag inhabits such a branch and an application node does not. That removes what kept the generated scope construction beside this module rather than on it, and the scope is now rebuilt there: two indices - names in scope, and processes whose quote is - four branches each witnessed by a declared term former, and the quote of a composite in scope while the quote of an undeclared atom is not. The rebuild is not a second construction resembling the first. The signature's polynomial is closed in the hand-written fixed point and the hand-written fixed point's induction principle lands in the signature's index, so the two are equal at both indices, and the descent procedure written against the hand-written fixed point decides membership of the signature's index with no second procedure and no second correctness proof. What the passage costs is stated rather than absorbed: a signature's branches are constructors of the presentation, so the atoms are declared nullary processes where the hand-written transformer took arbitrary predicates, and that restriction is the content of being language-generated." }
  , { area := "Scopes and Fixpoints"
      title := "The generator is a constructor of the formula language, in the frame of the generated logic"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Formula.lean: OSLFFormula.var / OSLFFormula.mu / OSLFFormula.emptyColl / OSLFFormula.cut / OSLFFormula.headed / size / closedAt / muFree / spatialFree / modalOnly / modalOnly_iff / positiveIn / negativeIn / shift / substAt / unfold / cutSplits / PredFrame / PredFrame.close / PredFrame.le_close / PredFrame.mem_close / PredFrame.close_mono / fullFrame / langSemUsing_eq_sem_of_modalOnly / semEnv / setoidFrame / semEnv_setoidInvariant / frameClosed_setoidFrame / equationFrameUsing_eq_setoidFrame; Mettapedia/OSLF/Formula.lean: FrameClosed / mem_semEnv_mu / semEnv_congr_of_closedAt / semEnv_substAt / semEnv_polarity / semEnv_mu_eq_unfold / semEnv_mu_le / semEnv_frame_irrelevant / frameClosed_equationFrameUsing / equationInvariant_scopeEnv_empty / equationFrameUsing / semEnv_equationInvariantUsing / langSemUsing / langFormulaSemUsing_apply_sem_of_modalOnly / sem_equationInvariantUsing / check / check_semEnv_sat_sound; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/SourceGenerator.lean: sourceScope / rhoScope / sourceScope_size / sourceScope_closed / sourceScope_positive / sourceScope_unfold / sem_sourceScope_iff / sourceScope_not_modalOnly / sourceScope_not_muFree / sourceScope_not_spatialFree / sourceScope_is_quote / sourceScope_is_quote_setoid / not_semEnv_headed_collection / semEnv_headed_of_equiv_setoid / semEnv_cut_of_split_setoid / sourceScope_unfold_setoid / sourceScope_step_setoid / semEnv_headed_of_equiv / semEnv_cut_of_split / sourceScope_unfold_equational / sourceScope_step / sourceScope_is_quote_equational / Specimen.atoms / Specimen.baseName / Specimen.baseName_in_scope / Specimen.baseName_sem / Specimen.droppedName_not_positional / Specimen.atomA_not_placed; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformSourceScope.lean: stopDeclaration_mem / quoteDeclaration_mem / dropDeclaration_mem / parDeclaration_mem / outDeclaration_mem / stop_hasSort / quote_hasSort / drop_hasSort / out_hasSort / bag_sortedParts / chain / chain_sorted / drop_chain_sortedParts / rawAtoms / scope / ambient_chain_zero / ambient_scope_eq / ambient_chain_one_not / atoms / atoms_stopped / atoms_emitting / chain_singleton / chain_in_scope / frame_separates / leftPart / rightPart / generatedScope_hasSort / platform_singletonDrop / generatedScope_le_formula / coerced_in_generatedScope / coerced_in_formula / sortedAtoms / chain_sorted_singleton / chain_in_sorted_scope / sorted_frame_separates / sortedPartAtoms / platform_sorted_singletonDrop / generatedScope_le_sorted_formula; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/ScopeComparison.lean: part / partAtoms / scopeFormula / atomicLayer / atomicLayer_le_generatedScope / sem_scopeFormula_iff_atomicLayer / sem_scopeFormula_le_generatedScope / equationPartAtoms / equationPartAtoms_left / equationPartAtoms_right / generatedScope_le_langSemUsing / generatedScope_le_semEnv_setoid / Specimen.baseName_in_layer / Specimen.baseName_sem / Specimen.coercedName_in_generatedScope / Specimen.coercedName_not_sem / Specimen.constructions_separate; Mettapedia/OSLF/Decidability.lean: semFuel / check_sat_iff_semFuel / semFuel_implies_sem; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratorLength.lean: reachable / reachable_size / sem_reachable_iff / check_reachable_chain_three / check_reachable_starved / stratum / stratum_values / stratum_superlinear; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/FormulaFixpoint.lean: transformer_forgets_generator; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/InitialModalSchema.lean: semEnv_eq_fold; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/EvidenceSemantics.lean: semEEnv / equationEvidenceFrameUsing / semEEnv_equationInvariantUsing; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/ConcreteHennessyMilnerBridge.lean: satisfiesEnv / satisfiesEnv_resp"
      note := "The addition to the syntax is exactly two constructors, and it was made only after the argument for it was proved rather than asserted: two syntactically distinct generators are equal as transformers, so generator length is not a function of a transformer at all. A generator denotes the intersection of the pre-fixed points of its body inside a frame, a class of predicates closed under arbitrary intersection, carried as a parameter; the raw reading uses the ambient powerset and the modulo-equations reading uses the equation-invariant predicates, which are the project's own notion of a predicate of the generated logic. Taking the fixed point there rather than in the powerset is what makes equation-invariance of a generated scope hold for every body, monotone or not, and keeps the interpretation into equation predicates total. Positivity is then needed for one thing only, the fixed point law, and it is decidable and kernel-reducible, so the bounded checker answers a generator by descent with exactly that law as its guard. The three other interpretations of the same syntax were carried through the same way: the evidence-valued reading takes its generator as a greatest lower bound in a frame of observations, the concrete Hennessy-Milner reading in the class the GSLT equations cannot see past, and the initial-algebra presentation gained the two constructors with its predicate algebra reindexed by scope environments, since a generator reads its body one binding deeper than itself. Statements that quantify over every formula and are false at a non-monotone generator now say so: observational indistinguishability, bisimulation invariance and transport, the translations into Hennessy-Milner and into modal logic, whose target languages have no fixpoint operator at all, and the evidence threshold bridge each range over the generator-free formulas, which is exactly the strength they had. A bisimulation map induces no homomorphism of the environment-indexed algebra, because a map on terms has no action on environments, so that route is stated on the base signature instead. The two formula languages are now one. The syntax carries the empty collection, the cut and a unary declared former beside the binder and the modalities, so the source's own scope generator -- a quote around a parallel composition each of whose parts is an atom or the drop of a name the generator already has -- is a formula of this language: eleven nodes, closed, positive in its bound variable, and therefore subject to the fixed point law, all by computation. The structural formers are read through the frame rather than beside it, which is what makes them connectives of this language: the frame gained a closure operator, monotone and above the predicate it closes, so the ambient reading of a cut is the positional decomposition and the equation reading is the separating conjunction modulo the equations, with invariance holding for the new formers by the closure landing in the frame. The cost is named rather than absorbed. A bisimulation preserves behaviour, not shape, so the invariance and frame-irrelevance statements now range over the modal fragment -- no generator and no structural connective -- which is what generator-free meant before the language had a cut, and the two notions are proved to agree exactly. And the ambient frame presents a cut's part as a singleton collection, so the generator's coercion step is a statement about the equation frame, where the declared collection algebra derives the singleton law. That step is now taken rather than deferred. A declared former is read up to the equations by the frame's own closure, so a one-element composition satisfies it exactly when the element does, and the generator's recursive step follows: a name already in the scope, dropped and composed with a part the right-hand predicate accepts, quotes to a name in the scope again, with the singleton law the one hypothesis it consumes. The separation between the two readings is stated as a theorem rather than as a checker verdict. In the ambient powerset the same formula at the same presentation and the same part predicates denotes exactly its base case, because the recursive disjunct asks a composition to be an application and no composition is one; in the frame the presentation's equations select, a whole chain of names is in it, each coding the previous one. The instance is the platform presentation's, and the sorting judgement the derived singleton law carries is discharged for the entire chain by induction on the grammar -- five introduction rules read off the declarations -- rather than by a separate decision at each level. What the scope contains is also bounded from above in both frames: everything in it is a quote, up to the equations in the generated logic and on the nose in the ambient powerset. The two constructions of the same rho name scope are now related rather than left side by side. In the ambient powerset the formula denotes the hand-written transformer's atoms-only layer exactly, an equality and not an inclusion, because the recursive disjunct asks a one-element composition to be an application. In the frame of a generated logic the formula's extension contains the whole hand-written fixed point, coercion included, as soon as the presentation identifies a one-element composition of a drop with that drop -- a condition asked for only at the names the scope contains, and discharged on the platform by an induction on the grammar showing every such name is a name of the presentation. The specimen separates the two readings at exactly the coercion: a coerced name is in the hand-written scope and outside the formula's ambient reading, and inside it in the generated logic. What is not claimed is the converse of the second statement, which is the membership question for equation classes; the hand-written descent decides membership for representatives, and modulo the reflection equation the size argument that makes it terminate is unavailable, so nothing here supplies it."
    }
  , { area := "Weighting"
      title := "Weights index derivations, not steps: the Prop-indexing defect and its repair"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/GSLT/Dynamics/EvidenceWeighting.lean: weightMap_proof_irrelevant / costMap_proof_irrelevant / EvidenceWeightMap / EvidenceCostMap / EvidencePath / evidenceAmplitude / evidenceTotalCost / EvidencePath.erase / EvidencePath.erase_length / Canary.oneStep / Canary.routes / Canary.tollByRoute / Canary.tollByRoute_separates / Canary.routes_erase_to_one_step / Canary.no_stepIndexed_weighting_separates / EvidenceWeightMap.ofStepIndexed / EvidenceCostMap.ofStepIndexed / ofStepIndexed_constant / Canary.tollByRoute_not_a_shadow / externalTotal / externalTotal_perm_invariant / adaptiveTotal / adaptiveTotal_nil / Adaptation.byPosition / Adaptation.adaptive_not_perm_invariant / Adaptation.external_is_perm_invariant; Mettapedia/GSLT/Dynamics/EvidenceWeighting.lean: adapt / adapt_zero / adaptiveTotal_adapt / adaptiveTotal_of_prefixBlind / adaptiveTotal_adapt_perm_invariant_of_prefixBlind / Adaptation.byPosition_not_prefixBlind / Adaptation.blinded_is_perm_invariant / binderCount / binderArity / ReadsOnlyMatch / byBinderArity / BinderArity.output_arity / BinderArity.input_arity / BinderArity.byBinderArity_not_readsOnlyMatch / BinderArity.byBinderArity_separates / BinderArity.readsOnlyMatch_cannot_separate; Mettapedia/GSLT/Dynamics/WeightCost.lean: WeightMap / CostMap; Mettapedia/GSLT/Core/ProofRelevantGSLT.lean: StepEvidence"
      note := "The weight and cost maps the tree already had are indexed by the step relation, which is a proposition, so proof irrelevance makes every one of them constant on derivations: a weighting of that shape cannot give two derivations of the same reduction different weights, whatever its author intends, and that is a property of the index type rather than of any particular map. Both statements are theorems and neither depends on any axiom. The repair uses the equipment already in the tree: a proof-relevant theory carries a type-valued evidence family whose inhabitants are the derivations, tied to the step relation so that no event is invented and none lost, and weight and cost maps indexed by that family can depend on which derivation was taken. Paths of derivations carry an amplitude and a total cost, and erase to ordinary rewrite paths of the same length, so the layer adds information and loses none. A theory with one reduction and two derivations of it is exhibited, with an evidence-indexed weighting that separates them and the proof that no step-indexed weighting can. The step-indexed layer is exhibited as the first-order shadow of this one: every step weighting casts an evidence weighting by forgetting which derivation was taken, every cast weighting is constant on derivations, and the canary's weighting is proved not to be cast by any of them, so the evidence layer is strictly larger rather than a relabelling. The external and internal forms of a weighting of alternatives are both written, and they are separated: the external total is invariant under permuting the alternatives, while an adaptive weighting that charges an alternative by how many were taken before it gives the same two alternatives different totals in the two orders, so internal adaptation makes the enumeration order observable. Summability is not a side condition for this presentation and the reason is structural rather than a dispensation — the alternatives a rule offers are a list, so the total is a finite sum — and a presentation whose alternatives are not finitely enumerated still needs it. Both of the items this row previously listed as unwritten are now written. The adaptive delta is a transformation rather than a comparison of totals: an internal weighting is an external one plus a correction that may read the prefix, the adapted total splits as the external total plus the correction's own adaptive total with nothing else added, and the zero correction changes nothing. That locates the failure of invariance exactly -- a correction blind to the prefix leaves the total invariant under permuting the alternatives however large it is, so what breaks invariance is the reading of the prefix and only that, and the witness that breaks it is proved not to be prefix-blind while its blinded form is proved invariant. Where-weights carry binder arities: a weight attached to one match reads the binder arity of the rule it matched, computed from the declared parameters rather than tabulated, and that weighting is proved not to factor through the bindings alone -- two declared formers with the same empty match and different binder arities are charged differently, while any weighting of the bindings alone charges them alike. What is not written and not claimed: The permutation-invariance result the plan names as the link target is not present in the tree under that name; the non-invariance theorem here is proved outright on its own witness rather than by linking to a substitute chosen for the resemblance of its name." }
  , { area := "Platform Presentation"
      title := "N-ary and persistent joins, Omega-valued where-guards, and the chess ply as join arity"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformEquations.lean: Sorted.parts_sorted / Sorted.swapped_sorted / Sorted.parts_equated / Sorted.splits / Sorted.splits_comm / Sorted.stop_sorted / Sorted.output_sorted / Sorted.empty_sorted / Sorted.singleton_law / Sorted.empty_is_stop / Sorted.stop_absorbs / Sorted.parts_equiv_output / parDeclaration_isCarrier / parDeclaration_isAlgebra / platform_flatten / platform_singleton / platform_emptyUnit / platform_unitElim / platform_usesCollection / sortedParts / platform_permInvariantOn / platform_cut_comm / platform_satisfiesModuloOver_cut / platform_emptyColl_reading; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformPresentation.lean: stopDeclaration / quoteDeclaration / parDeclaration / restVar / quoteLabel / tupleLabel / deliveredTuple / deliveredName / joinLabel / persistentJoinLabel / channelVars / valueVars / receiver / outputs / joinRule / persistentJoinRule / joinRule_guard / persistentJoinRule_guard / joinRule_consumes_receiver / persistentJoinRule_retains_receiver / joinRule_ne_persistentJoinRule / rhoPlatform / rhoPlatform_labels_nodup_pair / rhoPlatform_labels_nodup_three / tupleDeclaration_label_distinct / joinRule_mem / persistentJoinRule_mem / joinPos / joinRule_focus_one / joinRule_focus_two / joinRule_focus_three / participantVars / participantVars_length / joinRule_one_relyVars / joinRule_two_relyVars / joinRule_three_relyVars / joinRule_relyVars_head / joinRule_one_slotCount / joinRule_two_slotCount / joinRule_three_slotCount / joinRule_relyVars_declared / Guard.admitsOnce_fires / Guard.admitsOnce_fires_in_context / Guard.admitsNone_blocks / Guard.admitsTwice_fires_twice / Guard.persistent_fires_twice / Guard.plain_does_not_fire_twice / Chess.Ply / Chess.Ply.arity / Chess.Ply.rule / Chess.Ply.rule_mem / Chess.Ply.rule_eq_iff_arity_eq / Chess.Ply.arities_realised / Chess.castle_and_capture_share_arity / Chess.enPassant_unique_arity_three; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformSlotLaws.lean: channelVar_ne_valueVar / channelVar_ne_continuationVar / valueVar_ne_continuationVar / channelVar_ne_restVar / valueVar_ne_restVar / participantVars_succ / channelVars_succ / mem_participantVars_iff / mem_channelVars_iff / participantVars_nodup / channelVars_subset_participantVars / restVar_not_mem_participantVars / continuationVar_not_mem_participantVars / channelPatterns_length / outputs_succ / channelPatterns_succ / fvarNames_outputs / fvarNames_channelPatterns / contextFreeVars_receiver / contextFreeVars_joinRule / focusFreeVars_joinRule / eraseDups_of_nodup / joinRule_relyVars / joinRule_slotCount / joinRule_relyVars_declared / joinLabel_injective / persistentJoinLabel_injective / tupleLabel_injective / joinLabel_ne_persistentJoinLabel / joinLabel_ne_tupleLabel / persistentJoinLabel_ne_tupleLabel / fixedLabels / joinLabel_not_fixed / persistentJoinLabel_not_fixed / tupleLabel_not_fixed / generatedLabels / mem_generatedLabels_iff / generatedLabels_nodup / generatedLabels_disjoint / generated_not_fixed / generatedLabels_flatMap_nodup / rhoPlatform_labels_nodup; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/RedexPosition.lean: binderNames / binderNamesList / binderNames_eq / binderNamesList_eq / patternFvarNames_nil / flatMap_patternFvarNames_nil; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformValidation.lean: joinRule_premises / persistentJoinRule_premises / validateEquation_quoteDrop / validateRewrite_join / validateRewrite_persistentJoin / rhoPlatform_equations / rhoPlatform_rewrites_pair / rhoPlatform_validate"
      note := "The presentation is generated from the arities it supports rather than tabulated: a join of arity n computes its channel and value variables, its bag of participants, its continuation and its guard from n alone, and the persistent family differs from the plain one in exactly whether the receiver appears on the right, which is proved rather than named. Where-guards are relationQuery premises, so the firing condition is answered by the relation environment rather than by the term, and because that environment answers with a list of rows the guard is many-valued rather than Boolean: no rows blocks a join whose participants are all present, one row fires it once, two rows fire it twice, all three kernel-checked. The rules are contextual: each matches a parallel remainder and puts it back, so a join fires beside processes it does not touch, kernel-checked at a board carrying an idle process. The redex-position generator is run on the generated rules with nothing hand-written and returns the arity: a join of arity n relies on the remainder, its n channels and its n values, so it carries 2n+2 slots, checked at arities one, two and three, and every metavariable it uses is declared — including the remainder, which is the defect this tree's own communication rule has. The remainder is the parameter the contextual reading adds, and the slot family counts it. The specimen is the chess ply: its taxonomy is how many pieces of state must agree, two plies are performed by the same join exactly when they have that number in common, and the arities the taxonomy realises are exactly the three the presentation supports. The presentation now carries an equation theory, and it carries it as a declaration rather than as a list: a parallel carrier declaring a bag of processes, from which the bag laws are derived. Item 3 therefore runs on it. Permutation invariance on the collections the presentation sorts needs no hypothesis beyond that declaration; the cut is a separating conjunction on it, symmetric on every decomposition the presentation sorts, by the presentation's own derived law; and the structural connective's reading modulo those equations is that separating conjunction on the nose, with the empty bag as its unit former. The sorting judgement the derived law is conditioned on is discharged rather than only carried: the presentation declares a terminated process and a quote, so it has closed processes at all, and a concrete parallel composition of two of them is checked well sorted by the presentation's own declarations, its reordering likewise, the two equated by the derived law with no hypothesis left standing, and the cut's symmetry instantiated on that composition. The algebra is declared too, not only the carrier: the parallel bag flattens and its unit is the terminated process, so associativity, the singleton law, the unit law and unit absorption are derived from that single declaration, and all four are instantiated at sorted witnesses -- the composition of a terminated process and an output is proved equal to that output, by derived laws only. Persistence is now operational rather than syntactic: the persistent family's every successor fires again, and the plain family's none does, both kernel-checked. Two earlier defects are repaired. The bundle former is indexed by its arity, so a presentation supporting several arities declares distinct constructors rather than several under one name; distinctness is checked at the arity families used. And the calculus is reflective where it claimed to be: a join binds a name, and what reduction substitutes is the quote of the bundle, so the name sort is inhabited by reduction rather than vestigial. The collection kind of the rules is no longer a free parameter disconnected from the declared carrier; the rules and the carrier are the same bag. The presentation is now reflective in fact: it declares a drop beside its quote and carries the equation that a quote of a drop is the name dropped, so names are codes of processes rather than a sort standing beside them. Four of the eight items now run on it. Item one runs as a whole-presentation generator: twenty-four redex sites, every one of which declares every slot it mints, and the generated cube at the join has dimension two times the arity plus two, with the face cut out by one condition on the output slot. Item three runs as before. Item four runs on the presentation's own three formers -- the scope's quote, drop and composition are those declarations, not a vocabulary sharing their names -- with membership decided by descent, a positive instance through the coercion and a negative outside it. Item six runs on its declarations: the join binds one name and the output former binds none, so the where-weight that reads binder arity separates them where no weighting of the match alone can. Item five runs on it too, by the route the presentation allows: its rules carry relationQuery premises, which the closed-subsystem condition correctly refuses since such a premise makes no recursive call, so agreement of the authored and instrumented step relations is settled by computation instead. The observer theorems are now stated at the level they need -- two step relations agreeing on a set closed under them -- with the observer extension one way of obtaining such a set and this presentation another. The fragment here is inert, and that is a fact about the presentation rather than about the terms chosen: every rule of it matches at a bag, so no term headed by a declared operation is a redex. Item two runs on it as well, so all six of items one to six do. The platform's contexts are parallel remainders and therefore bags, its context category has relative pushouts for every span and every bound, the congruence holds there for every context with nothing assumed, and the reaction rule the labelled transitions are built from is checked in the kernel to be the engine's own. The slot laws are no longer three instances. They are proved at every arity: the context of a join's redex is the parallel remainder together with every participant's channel and value and the receiver's repeated channel names, its focus is the continuation binder, and the generator's deduplication removes exactly those repetitions -- so the rely parameters are the remainder and the participants, and the slot count is two per participant plus the remainder and the output, for every arity. Three obligations had to be met and each is real. The scan of a redex's siblings is computed for a list a generator produces rather than one written out, by two lemmas about skipping one index of an indexed traversal. The generated names are told apart by decimal printing being injective, which the tree already proves from a decoder, together with the prefixes differing in their first character. And the deduplication is computed rather than assumed, from the participant list having no repetitions and every channel name being a participant name. That every metavariable a slot is minted for is declared is proved at every arity too, from the generated type context. The presentation's own validation gate is discharged too, and not by a convention: LanguageDef.validate resolves every cross-reference between types, constructors, relations and syntax parameters, rejects a name declared twice, and rejects the silent-wildcard shapes an authored rule can fall into -- and the platform presentation passes it, kernel-checked. Two of the validator's helpers stood in the way and both are now repaired at the framework rather than worked around: the free-variable scan recurses over a nested pattern list by well-founded recursion and the binder scan recurses through an attached list, so neither reduces in the kernel, and structurally recursive counterparts with their agreement theorems now sit beside them. A validation run is therefore a kernel computation rather than a compiled evaluation, which is what the arity-indexed bundle former was introduced for. Constructor distinctness is a law rather than two instances as well: the three generated former families are injective in the arity, pairwise distinct, and distinct from the five fixed formers, so a presentation over any repetition-free arity list declares no name twice. What is not written and not claimed: the validation gate itself is discharged at the arity family the tree uses rather than for every arity list -- the generic run needs the constructor labels proved disjoint from the generated *variable* names too, which is the same first-character argument one level further out and is not done." }
  , { area := "Substitutability Parity"
      title := "Theorem 1 on the platform's own step relation, and the logical metric's enumeration dependence"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformSubstitutability.lean: platformStep / platformStep_imageFinite / platform_substitutability_forward / platform_substitutability_of_predFinite / logicalRank / logicalRank_isSome_iff / logicalRank_isSome_congr / Enumeration.same_pairs_ranked / Enumeration.rank_depends_on_enumeration / Enumeration.ranks_computed / Backward.sources_distinct / Backward.distinct_sources_one_target / Backward.sources_step / ConcreteMetric.headedBy / ConcreteMetric.atomSem / ConcreteMetric.sem_atom_iff / ConcreteMetric.separates / ConcreteMetric.separates_sound / ConcreteMetric.catalogue / ConcreteMetric.enumeration / ConcreteMetric.rank_computed / ConcreteMetric.swapped_rank_computed / ConcreteMetric.rank_depends_on_catalogue / ConcreteMetric.same_pairs_ranked / ConcreteMetric.rank_witness_separates / boundedStep / boundedStep_imageFinite / boundedStep_predFinite / platform_substitutability_bounded / Bounded.successor / Bounded.domain / Bounded.board_steps / Bounded.parity; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/SubstitutabilityTheorem1.lean: Theorem1SubstitutabilityEquiv / theorem1_substitutability_forward / theorem1_substitutability_imageFinite"
      note := "Theorem 1's two sides are related on the platform presentation's own step relation. The forward direction, behavioural equivalence implying sameness of native types, holds outright. For the converse one of the two image-finiteness hypotheses is free and the other is not, and the difference is stated rather than smoothed over: the platform computes its successors into a list, so forward image-finiteness is a theorem about this presentation instead of an assumption about rho, while backward image-finiteness is a named hypothesis, which is the honest position given that this tree already proves it false for rho's own step relation. The logical metric is the second half. A metric refining logical equivalence ranks a pair by the first formula of a listing that separates them, and the two things that word first controls behave differently: the relation induced, being separated at all, is proved independent of the listing whenever two listings enumerate the same formulas, while the rank itself is proved dependent on it, with the same two formulas in the other order giving the same pair the ranks one and zero. So the equivalence Theorem 1 is about is an invariant of the logic and any metric refining it is an artefact of the enumeration. The metric is now computed rather than only characterised. The separation test is read off the semantics instead of posited beside it: at an atomic formula the semantics is the atom reading, so a decidable atom reading decides separation in both directions - which a bounded checker does not give, being sound for satisfaction and silent otherwise, and keeping the enumeration atomic is what buys the exactness. The catalogue is the presentation's own formers in a fixed order, and two terms of the presentation, the terminated process and an output on its quote, are ranked against it: the first listed former that tells them apart is found at index one, and at index zero under a catalogue with its first two entries exchanged, while the two catalogues list the same formulas and therefore rank the same pairs. The formula the rank points at is then shown to separate the two terms in the semantics rather than in the test. Parity now holds in both directions where it can. On a bounded domain the step relation is image-finite forwards and backwards for the same reason -- a subset of a finite set is finite -- so behavioural equivalence and sameness of native types coincide there with nothing assumed, and the domain carrying the presentation's own reaction is exhibited so the statement is not about an empty relation. A bounded domain is what a running system has rather than a convenience. What is not written and not claimed: the unrestricted backward image-finiteness hypothesis has no instance -- which is now said exactly rather than left as an open obligation. The two hypotheses are not on the same footing. Forward image-finiteness is a theorem, because the platform computes its successors into a list. Backward image-finiteness is supplied by nothing the platform has, and the step relation is visibly many-to-one: a continuation that discards what it receives sends every choice of transmitted value to one successor, and two such sources, distinct and both stepping, are exhibited with the same successor. So the converse is stated as the conditional it is, and it is not instantiated here." }
