      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/ObserverExtension.lean: answerSort / buildLabel / projectablePositions / askDeclaration / argsDeclaration / getDeclaration / buildDeclaration / openedRules / instrumentSorts / instrumentDeclarations / instrumentRules / openingRule / projectionRule / buildRule / observerExtension / mem_terms_of_mem / askDeclaration_mem / argsDeclaration_mem / buildDeclaration_mem / answerSort_declared / buildRule_mem / openedRules_mono / step_mono / step_of_base / ObAdmissible / no_opening_for_minting / no_instrument_rules_for_minting / instrumentLabels / adjoinedLabels / AdministrativeFresh / instrumentRules_cases / matchPattern_adjoined_eq_nil / rewriteAt_eq_of_authored_head / Gap.withC_steps / Gap.withD_no_step / Gap.open_then_build / Gap.inertPair_fresh / Gap.collidingPair_not_fresh / Gap.inertPair_conservative / askLabel_ne_self / buildLabel_ne_getLabel / getLabel_index_injective / matchRel_apply_args / matchRel_apply_head / argPatterns_length / headed_of_openingRule_match / argVars_length / argVars_nodup / openingRule_match_of_headed / openingRule_match_iff / projectionRule_right / projectionRule_exposes / projectionRule_delivers_of_match / openingRule_delivers_of_match; Mettapedia/OSLF/MeTTaIL/DecimalNames.lean: repr_injective / prefixed_injective / literal_ne / prefixed_ne_literal / prefixed_range_nodup; Mettapedia/OSLF/MeTTaIL/LinearMatch.lean: mergeBindings_of_fresh / matchArgs_fvars / find?_of_mem_of_nodup / mergeBindings_subset / matchRel_fvar_shape / matchArgsRel_fvars_inversion; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/ObserverBisimilarity.lean: Setting / computedStep / authoredStep / instrumentedStep / steps_agree / AgreeingFragment / AgreeingFragment.closed_second / Setting.agreeingFragment / restrict / stepBisimulation_first_of_second / stepBisimulation_second_of_first / bisimilar_iff / boxFree / semEnv_agree / sem_agree / separates_iff / box_not_forwardOnly / Instance.setting / Instance.fragment / Instance.readings_agree / Instance.canStep_separates / Instance.canStep_separates_instrumented; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/ObserverReconstruction.lean: step_of_premiseFree_match / match_of_step / opening_step / projection_step / adjoined_match_forces_head / step_dichotomy / argsHeaded_target_source / askLabel_ne_argsLabel / premisesAt_nil_eq / authored_premiseFree_target_not_argsHeaded / IsCongruence / Avoids / EvaluatorAvoids / premisesAt_avoids / authored_target_not_argsHeaded / evaluatorAvoids_of_barren / evaluatorAvoids_fails / PremiseAvoids / evaluatorAvoids_of_env / RulesAvoid / stepAt_avoids / premisesAt_avoids_full / premiseAt_avoids / authored_step_not_argsHeaded / Smuggling.carrier_fresh / Smuggling.cut_reaches_bundle / Smuggling.reaching_bundle_does_not_determine_head / Smuggling.drainRule_has_congruence / AuthoredRulesTame / reads_head_iff / Instrument / IsBundle / IsInstrumentBisimulation / isInstrumentBisimulation_eq / isInstrumentBisimulation_not_total / head_agreement / opening_response / argument_agreement / getLabel_mem_adjoinedLabels / ReadableHead / ReadableByKit / ReadableByKitList / readableByKit_labels / reconstruction / IsVariable / RigidHeads / LeftHeadDeclared / LeftHeadsDeclared / ObserverSetting / Determinacy.carrier_fresh / Determinacy.request_has_two_responses / Determinacy.projection_response_not_determined / Determinacy.carrier_not_rigid / Citation.carrier_fresh / Citation.carrier_rigid / Citation.carrier_not_cited / Citation.rigidity_alone_insufficient / authored_no_match_adjoined_head / instrument_step_is_adjoined / adjoined_projection_match_forces / projection_step_forces / projection_response / Interference.transition_does_not_determine_head / Interference.absorbing_step_reaches_no_bundle / Interference.opening_step_reaches_bundle / Interference.absorbing_fresh; Mettapedia/OSLF/MeTTaIL/OccurringLabels.lean: labels / labelsList / labels_liftBVars / labels_instantiateBVar / bindingLabels / labels_applyBindings / labelsList_mono / bindingLabels_mergeBindings / bindingLabels_matchRel / bindingLabels_matchPattern / premiseLabels / bindingLabels_matchRelationArgument / bindingLabels_matchRelationArgs / labelsList_builtinRelationTuples / bindingLabels_relationQueryStep; Mettapedia/OSLF/MeTTaIL/LinearMatch.lean: applyBindings_fvars"
      note := "The extension is a transformation of presentations: authored sorts, grammar, equations and rewrites are retained exactly, and per opened constructor a fresh sort for its argument bundle, four administrative formers and their rules are adjoined, so the extended theory is an ordinary presentation in which every adjoined rule cites only declared constructors. The instruments are constructor names read against the presentation's own grammar rather than a table written beside it, so an instrument cannot cite a constructor the theory does not declare or disagree with it about arity, and the argument former is freely adjoined over exactly the declared argument sorts. The build former is adjoined with them: what an opening takes apart can be put back together, kernel-checked on a unary constructor in both directions, so the observer's kit is not a one-way mirror. Projection is generated for the positions whose declared parameter is a term of a base sort; a binder position is excluded because projecting one would hand back an open body whose sort the presentation does not declare. Steps are proved monotone in the instrument set, the minting apparatus is excluded by an explicit admissibility condition so no token acquires a destructor, projection or build former — stated for what it is, a condition on the instrument set rather than a proof of unforgeability, since free adjunction cannot deliver unforgeability and a theory whose tokens are forgeable without any observer stays forgeable — and the gap is witnessed concretely: two inert nullary constructors that no context separates in the authored theory are separated by one opening request once the instrument is held. Freshness of the administrative vocabulary is a decidable condition on the presentation rather than a convention, and it is what buys conservativity: on a term headed by an authored operation the extension rewrites exactly as the authored theory does, with the same results, order and multiplicity, so the observer gains instruments and changes nothing about what the theory already did. The condition is discharged by computation on the worked presentation and exhibited failing on one that already declares a request former. Monotonicity of bisimilarity is now settled, and it is settled as an equality rather than an inclusion. On a fragment of terms headed by the authored vocabulary and closed under its own steps, the instrumented step relation and the authored one are the same relation, because the conservativity theorem equates the successor lists; so a bisimulation for one restricts to a bisimulation for the other in both directions, and bisimilarity on the fragment is unchanged by the instruments. The same equality carries the logic: for generator-free formulas that do not look backwards, the two readings of a formula agree at every term of the fragment, and a formula separates two of its terms in one reading exactly when it does in the other. The instrument set is named in every one of those statements, which is the index an adequacy claim has to carry. The boundary is named too and is not crossed: the future modality stays inside a step-closed fragment and the past modality does not, since a term's predecessors need not lie in the fragment, so the past modality is outside the fragment of the logic the theorem is about. None of it is carried and never met: a presentation with two nullary formers and one rule between them discharges every condition of the setting by its own declarations, the two terms form the fragment because the second is stuck, and the formula asking whether anything happens holds at one and fails at the other in both readings. The descent that a reconstruction argument runs on now has its first step as a law rather than as a specimen: the opening request for a constructor, placed beside a term in the cut, matches that constructor's opening rule only when the term is an application of that constructor at the declared arity. So the instrument reads the head, for every constructor of every presentation. The converse holds too, and generically: the opening rule is linear -- each argument metavariable minted once, because the generator mints them from an index and decimal printing is injective -- so the sibling bindings never conflict and the match succeeds whenever the head matches. That obligation is discharged at the generality it has rather than at this rule: merging fresh bindings always succeeds, and a list of distinct metavariables matches any list of terms of the same length, so any generated linear rule fires on the shape it names. The two halves together are an iff: the instrument reads the head exactly. The second descent step is a law too: the projection request for a position matches its rule, and applying the bindings the match produces to the rule's right-hand side delivers the argument at that position -- which is the observer learning what the constructor was applied to. It rests on the same linearity, together with a binding list with distinct names being a lookup table, so that a match determines what the right-hand side evaluates to. Reconstruction now has all three of its ingredients in the tree -- head-reading as an iff, argument exposure, and the descent principle the admissible-equation conditions supply -- and what remains is the bisimulation argument that assembles them, which is not claimed. Both descent steps now hold at the level of steps and not only of matches, which is the level a bisimulation argument works at. The distance is crossed as a law rather than at these two rules: step_of_premiseFree_match proves that a rule with no premises steps exactly when its left-hand side matches, in any presentation, and the generated administrative rules are premise-free by construction. So opening_step takes the request beside a term headed by its constructor to that constructor's argument bundle, and projection_step takes the projection request to the argument at its position, both as transitions of the extended presentation. The delivery now travels with the match rather than beside it: openingRule_match_of_headed reports what applying the bindings yields, resting on applyBindings_fvars, which is the generic fact that a linear match's bindings are a lookup table recovering exactly what the minted variables matched. Reconstruction itself -- bisimilarity in the full extension coinciding with the equations on closed terms -- remains open and is not claimed. Two things are missing, and they are named rather than described as documented. The first is settled, and settled negatively: observing a transition does not determine the head, and freshness does not repair it. An authored rule whose left-hand side is a bag with a tail variable fires on any bag containing its redex and carries the request along, which is exactly the shape rho's join rule has. transition_does_not_determine_head exhibits that on the smallest presentation with that shape, whose administrative vocabulary is fresh by computation. What the failure points at is the repair, and both signs of it are checked in the kernel: the observable is the transition's target rather than its existence, since only the opening rule builds a term headed by the constructor's argument former - absorbing_step_reaches_no_bundle shows the interfering step reaches no bundle, and opening_step_reaches_bundle shows the opening step reaches exactly the one opening_step names. The general half of that observable is now proved. Among the rules the extension adjoins, the request's own opening rule is the only one that can fire beside an authored term, and when it fires it reads the head: adjoined_match_forces_head, for any presentation, with the other two adjoined shapes excluded because they ask for an application while the cut is a collection, and an opening rule for a different constructor excluded because it would have to read its own request out of a term headed by an authored operation. Lifted to steps by step_dichotomy, a transition out of the instrumented cut either used an authored rule or read the head, so the interference is confined to the authored half exactly. Closing that half means showing no authored rule can build a target headed by the argument former, and the law that question needed now exists. OccurringLabels supplies the label-occurrence facts the Engine and premise layer needs - that layer being what it adds, since the Pattern-level metatheory already existed in GSLT/LanguageDef/ConstructorSupport.lean in Prop-valued containment form and should be derived from it rather than restated - namely three closure facts: lifting de Bruijn indices changes no label, eliminating a bound level introduces only the labels of the two patterns involved, and applying bindings introduces only the labels of the pattern and of the values substituted. The last is the one with content, since applyBindings eliminates a binder in the subst case and splices a bound collection into a rest position, and both are covered, with both signs checked on each. argsHeaded_target_source applies it: a target headed by the argument former forces that label into the rule's right-hand side or into the bindings the match and the premises produced. The companion law is there too - matching binds only labels of the term it matched, proved by mutual induction over the three matching relations, with merging shown to introduce nothing - so the premise-free authored case is closed: authored_premiseFree_target_not_argsHeaded shows no premise-free authored rule can build the bundle, since its target's labels come from its right-hand side and from what it matched, and freshness separates both from the argument former. Its two well-formedness hypotheses are stated as conditions on the presentation, which is what they are. The premise-bearing case is now covered too, under a condition on the surroundings that is stated for what it is. The naive form of that condition is wrong and was corrected by trying to satisfy it: forbidding the whole administrative vocabulary in the bindings is false, since a rule may perfectly well bind a metavariable to the opening request standing beside the term, so the request's label does reach the bindings in ordinary use. What must not reach them is the bundle former alone, and EvaluatorAvoids forbids exactly that one label. premisesAt_avoids carries it along a premise list whose premises take no steps, and authored_target_not_argsHeaded then closes the case, covering rho's join rule, whose only premise is a relation query. Congruence premises are excluded because they recurse into the step relation, which is a different induction. The condition has both signs witnessed: an evaluator producing nothing satisfies it, and one handing back a bundle violates it, so it is neither vacuous nor free. That condition is now discharged rather than assumed. The three label bounds it needed are proved - one relation argument binds only labels of the value it read, a row binds only labels of the row, and a relation query introduces only what its row carried - so evaluatorAvoids_of_env reduces the whole condition to the relation environment's own rows, the built-in relations being shown to echo the query's own arguments and introduce nothing. guard_evaluatorAvoids then discharges it for rho's own guard, whose single row holds channel constants. The premise's own patterns enter the condition because a built-in relation echoes the query's arguments back as a row, so a query mentioning the label could recover it with no help from the environment; that was found by trying to state the condition without it. Congruence premises are covered too, where the question is well posed: stepAt_avoids with premisesAt_avoids_full and premiseAt_avoids is a mutual induction over the step relation and the two premise relations, showing that a presentation whose rules cannot write a label never produces it, congruence premises included, and authored_step_not_argsHeaded applies that to the authored theory. That law does not transfer to the extension, and the reason is structural rather than a gap: the opening rule writes the bundle former, which is its whole purpose, so the rules-avoid hypothesis is false of the extension by construction. A congruence premise of an authored rule can therefore reach an opening rule and carry a bundle back out, and that is now settled rather than open: Smuggling does it in one step, from a cut whose term is authored and is not an application of the constructor the request names, on a presentation whose administrative vocabulary is fresh by computation. So the no-stepping-premises hypothesis of authored_target_not_argsHeaded is necessary rather than convenient - dropped, the conclusion is false - and reaching the bundle does not determine the head either once premises may step. Rho's join rule satisfies the hypothesis, its only premise being a relation query, which is why the argument reaches that presentation. All of it combines into one statement, reads_head_iff: on a presentation whose authored rules are tame - no stepping premises, nothing mentioning the bundle former, right-hand sides citing only declared constructors, each of which a canary showed necessary - an opening request beside a term reaches that constructor's bundle exactly when the term is an application of the constructor at the declared arity. That is the match-level openingRule_match_iff lifted from one rule to a whole presentation and its step relation, which is the level a bisimulation argument works at. Rho meets those conditions by proof rather than by argument from the shape of its rules: rhoPlatform_tame discharges all three at every arity list, not at one, its two rule families having a single relation-query premise apiece that mentions no constructor, and right-hand sides citing only the quote former and the arity's own tuple and join formers, each of which the presentation declares. The bisimulation argument is begun, and begun with the right notion rather than a reduction bisimilarity: IsInstrumentBisimulation relates terms tested by the same instrument, every clause naming the instrument set, with the bundle former as a barb, and without the barbs the matching step could be any step at all so that reaching a bundle on one side would say nothing about the other. Equality inhabits the notion and the total relation does not, the latter refuted on the gap canary's two inert constructors, so it is neither vacuous nor trivial. head_agreement is its first consequence: related terms are applications of the same constructor, obtained by asking the left term which constructor it is and reading the barb on the answer the right term must give. What remains is the descent from heads to arguments and the induction that turns it into equality. Descent needs a projection request's response to be determined rather than merely matched, and that is now known to be false in general rather than merely unproved: Determinacy exhibits a presentation with fresh administrative vocabulary where an authored rule with a bare metavariable on the left answers the request with whatever it likes, alongside the projection rule's own answer, so the request has two responses. RigidHeads names the condition that excludes exactly that shape, and nothing weaker will do, since every other left-hand side shape is already excluded - an apply cannot match an adjoined head because freshness separates the labels, and a collection, lambda or subst cannot match an application at all. rhoPlatform_rigidHeads discharges it for rho at every arity list, both rule families matching on a bag. The five conditions the item had accumulated are now one structure, ObserverSetting, rather than five loose preconditions that a downstream use could silently drop, and rhoPlatform_observerSetting discharges the whole of it for rho with the output former opened: freshness by computation, the guard by guard_evaluatorAvoids, tameness and rigidity at every arity list, and arity agreement because exactly one declaration is opened. reads_head_iff and head_agreement take the bundle. A sixth condition was then found the same way, before the inversion was attempted rather than after: rigidity alone does not determine the response. Citation exhibits a presentation where freshness holds and rigidity holds and the projection request still has two answers, because a left-hand side can be an application - hence rigid - whose head is a label the presentation never declared, and freshness constrains only the labels a presentation declares, never the labels a rule uses. LeftHeadsDeclared excludes exactly that and is now the sixth field of ObserverSetting, discharged for rho at every arity list because both rule families match on a bag. The authored half of the inversion those two conditions buy is proved: authored_no_match_adjoined_head shows no authored rule matches a term headed by an adjoined label at all - its left-hand side is not a variable so it does not match everything, and if it is an application its head is declared while the request's head is adjoined, which freshness separates, and every other left-hand side shape cannot match an application. instrument_step_is_adjoined lifts that to transitions: whatever answers an instrument's request, it is the kit answering rather than the presentation. The adjoined half is proved too: adjoined_projection_match_forces settles which member of the kit answers, the opening rule matching on a collection while a request is an application, the build rule carrying a different bracketed prefix, and the projection rule's own inner bundle former pinning the constructor before its index is consulted, so the label-collision condition that looked necessary is not - the inner former settles the constructor first. projection_step_forces puts the halves together: a transition out of a projection request used the projection rule for that constructor at that index and nothing else. What is left is what the answering rule returns. The inversion says which rule answered; the descent needs what it handed back, and projectionRule_exposes exhibits a binding list with the delivery property while the inversion supplies one that matches. That gap is closed by matchArgsRel_fvars_inversion, which is the missing half of the matcher's inversion API: every match of a list of distinct metavariables binds each to the term at its position, binds nothing else, and binds no name twice, the three facts proved in one induction because each step needs the previous two. projectionRule_delivers_of_match then applies to the bindings an inversion actually hands back rather than to a binding list exhibited separately, and projection_response reads: the projection instrument returns the argument at its position. openingRule_delivers_of_match is the bag-side companion, so both instruments now deliver from any match rather than from one exhibited alongside, the pairing of request against request being forced because the alternative would need the term to be the request itself. projection_response also now reads its arity condition off ObserverSetting rather than restating it, so the two cannot drift. The descent is assembled: argument_agreement shows related terms are applications of the same constructor and their arguments are related, position by projectable position, obtained by asking both terms which constructor they are, reading the barb on the answers, and then projecting one position out of both bundles. Every step of it is a statement about what any match binds, so nothing rests on a binding list exhibited apart from the one in hand. The position must be projectable, which is a limit of the kit rather than of the proof: projecting a binder position would hand back an open body whose sort the presentation does not declare, so the descent reaches exactly the positions the observer can read. The induction closes it: reconstruction shows terms related by an instrument bisimulation, both reachable by the present kit all the way down, are equal. ReadableByKit names that fragment - every head an opened constructor of matching arity, every position of it projectable, hereditarily - and it is narrow for two reasons, both properties of the kit rather than of the argument. Only apply nodes are reachable, because the kit opens declared constructors and a collection is a former of the carrier rather than a declared constructor, so parallel composition is unreadable and a calculus whose terms are bags lies entirely outside it. And a binder position has no projection rule, because projecting one would hand back an open body whose sort the presentation does not declare. Hereditary readability makes this bite hard: at the one rho setting instantiated here a single constructor is opened, so the fragment has no inhabitants at all and reconstruction is a theorem about the free apply-algebra over the opened signature with no instance yet exhibited. What is missing is instruments rather than proof - an opening instrument for the cut former, and an abstraction sort with an instantiation instrument for binder positions, each an adjunction of the kind the extension already performs. Separately, relating equality on that fragment to a larger equational theory is not done: the terms are equal on the nose and an =E over them is a further step. The item stays in progress." }
  , { area := "Equation Semantics"
      title := "The cut is a connective of the structural language, and its reading modulo the equations is the separating conjunction"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/Formula.lean: Formula.emptyColl / Formula.cut / satisfiesOver / Certificate.emptyColl / Certificate.cut / Formula.finitelyCertifiable; Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/EquationInvariance.lean: satisfiesModuloOver / satisfiesModuloUsing_equationInvariant / satisfiesModuloOver_of_satisfiesOver; Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/SeparatingConjunction.lean: PositionalConj / SepConj / PermInvariantOn / permInvariantOn_of_bagCarrier / sepConj_comm / sepConj_comm_of_bagCarrier / inertSpan / CollectionFree / collections_indistinguishable / no_collectionFree_formula_separates_empty_bag / emptyColl_separates_empty_bag / singleton_bags_distinct / satisfiesOver_cut / satisfiesModuloOver_cut / satisfiesModuloOver_cut_comm / satisfiesModuloUsing_cut_reaches_element / SepConj monoid laws: Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/SeparatingConjunction.lean: SplitCongruent / Emp / sepConj_emp_right_of / sepConj_emp_left_of / of_sepConj_emp_right / sepConj_assoc_right / sepConj_assoc_left / sepConj_mono"
      note := "A term satisfies the cut connective when it decomposes modulo the equations, not only in the presentation it is written in. Every positional split is such a decomposition and the converse fails: the positional reading of a two-element bag is not even symmetric, while the separating reading is, as soon as the tag supplies permutation invariance. For a presentation with a declared sorted bag carrier that invariance is a derived law rather than a hypothesis, and it is now actually discharged: the law is conditioned on the collection being sorted at the carrier's declared category, so a statement asking for permutation invariance at every element list asks for what no sorted presentation supplies, and the conditioned form carries exactly the sorting judgement the derived law is conditioned on. The cut is now a connective of the structural-modal formula language rather than a predicate combinator beside it, together with a former for the empty collection, and neither was added on taste. Before them the language could not see inside a collection at all: with nothing reducing, no formula of the collection-free fragment separates any two collections, since every other former either ignores the term or matches an application node while the modal formers read the reduction span. The fragment cannot tell the empty bag from a one-element bag; one formula of the extended language can. The payoff is that the separating reading is derived rather than posited. Read on the term as written the connective is the positional conjunction, and read through the layer that already interprets the spatial former on some equivalent representative it is the separating conjunction of its two sub-readings, both on the nose. Symmetry then comes from the presentation's own derived permutation law, which is now discharged rather than assumed. No third former for a singleton is added: the cut reaches a collection's elements through the presentation's singleton law, so naming a one-element collection is the cut of the element's formula with the empty one. Note for readers of earlier status notes: the OSLF entry was already equation-aware before this row — langOSLFUsing goes through langGSLTUsing and gsltModuloEquations, whose setoid is generated by EquationInstance together with DerivedInstance, so the tag-derived collection laws were already in it and the modalities were already semanticDiamond over EquationPredicate. The connective now has its monoid laws and not only its symmetry. Associativity in both directions, and the unit law against the empty collection, are proved from one named property of the equation theory -- that replacing one part of a composition by an equivalent part leaves the composition equivalent -- and the connective is monotone in both arguments. Half of each unit law needs nothing at all: a composition satisfying a predicate splits as itself beside the empty composition. Naming that property rather than assuming permutation invariance everywhere is the same discipline the symmetry law follows: a presentation supplies it or it does not. On the rho platform the property's ingredients are present, since the parallel carrier declares a collection algebra that flattens with the terminated process for its unit, from which associativity, the singleton law, the unit law and unit absorption are all derived and instantiated at sorted witnesses." }
  , { area := "Equation Semantics"
      title := "Equation instances that read the equation's own type context, and what the permissive ones cost"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/GSLT/LanguageDef/SortedEquationInstance.lean: SortedBindings / SortedEquationInstanceAt / SortedEquationInstance / equationInstance_of_sortedEquationInstance / SortedEquationGenerator / equationGenerator_of_sorted / SortedEquationContextStep / equationContextStep_of_sorted / SortedEquationEquiv / equationEquiv_of_sortedEquationEquiv / sortedEquationEquiv_invariant / headedBy_fill_congr / sortedDerivedInstance_equivalent / sortedEquationSetoid / StepModuloSortedEquations / gsltModuloSortedEquations / stepModuloEquations_of_sorted / stepModuloSortedEquations_of_step; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformEquationDiscipline.lean: quoteDropEquation_declares_a_name / matcher_instantiates_name_by_a_process / stop_equated_with_quotedDropOfStop / stop_is_a_process / no_quote_separating_invariant / quote_of_drop_of_a_name / QuoteHeaded / stop_not_quoteHeaded / quotedDropOfStop_quoteHeaded / process_not_quoteHeaded / name_is_quoteHeaded / derived_not_quoteHeaded / sortedInstance_quoteHeaded_iff / quoteHeaded_respects / stop_not_sortedEquated / quoteHeaded_sortedEquationInvariant / quoteHeaded_mem_sortedFrame / quoteHeaded_not_mem_frame / frames_separate / every_pattern_equated_with_its_quote / permissive_quote_predicate_is_trivial / stop_not_in_sortedScope / permissive_bound_refutes_nothing; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/SortedEquationFrame.lean: langSortedGSLTUsing / langSortedSemanticReducesUsing / langSemanticReducesUsing_of_sorted / SortedEquationAtomSemUsing / sortedEquationPredicate / sortedEquationAtomSemUsing / sortedEquationFrameUsing / mem_sortedEquationFrame_of_mem_equationFrame / langSortedSemUsing / sortedEquationInvariant_scopeEnv_empty / sortedEquationFrameUsing_eq_setoidFrame / semEnv_sortedEquationInvariantUsing / frameClosed_sortedEquationFrameUsing / langSortedFormulaSemUsing / langSortedFormulaSemUsing_apply"
      note := "An authored equation carries a type context: it declares, for each schema variable, the sort the variable ranges over. The instance relation that generates a presentation's equation theory does not read it. It matches a side of the equation against a term with the ordinary pattern matcher, so a variable declared to range over one sort is instantiated by any pattern at all. On the rho platform the consequence is exhibited rather than described: the reflection equation declares its variable to be a name, the matcher instantiates it by the terminated process -- which the presentation declares to be a process and no rule declares to be a name -- and the generated theory therefore equates that process with the name that quotes its drop, in one step at the root, kernel-checked at the matcher. What that costs is stated as an impossibility rather than left as an open obligation: no predicate telling a quote from a non-quote is equation-invariant, so no such predicate is a predicate of the generated logic, and that is why the negative half of a scope statement is proved in the ambient powerset in this tree rather than in the equation frame. It is not a missing lemma; the statement the lemma would have is false while instances are unsorted. The disciplined relation is then supplied beside the permissive one. A sorted instance is one whose substitution puts, at each variable the equation declares, an object pattern sorted at the declared type -- so neither a pending explicit substitution nor an open collection tail, and typed by the presentation's own grammar. The sorted theory is contained in the generated one, so every negative about it is a statement about the discipline and not about a different presentation, and a predicate respected by every disciplined generator in every context is respected by the whole disciplined theory. Half of that obligation is discharged once for all invariants: outside the hole a predicate of the head former cannot tell the two sides of a generator apart, because the filled term's head is the context's. On the platform the discipline buys exactly the predicate the permissive theory cannot have. No rule declares a quote to be a process, so a process is never a quote in any typing context; only the quote declares a name, so a term of the name sort at the empty context is a quote; and every presentation-derived law relates compositions, unit constants or processes, none of which is a quote -- the singleton law included, because its own sorting judgement forces the element it exposes to be a process. So a disciplined authored instance has quotes on both sides and a derived one has quotes on neither, the predicate is an invariant of the disciplined theory, and the identification the permissive theory makes is absent from it. Same presentation, same equation, and the discipline is the whole difference. The disciplined theory is then carried up to the OSLF layer, so the separation is visible where it decides what a formula can say. The presentation's disciplined generated theory is a GSLT with the same authored step and the smaller equivalence, its steps are steps of the permissive one, and every authored step is one of its steps, so it is not smaller for want of equations. Its frame of predicates is built the same way as the permissive frame and contains it, since invariance under a larger equivalence is a stronger demand; the containment is proved rather than assumed. And it is strict on this presentation: the quote predicate is a member of the disciplined frame and provably not a member of the permissive one. The frame is the only thing that changed. The metatheory is then inherited rather than recopied, because the construction it needs is written once at the generality it actually holds. A frame of predicates is decided by an equivalence on terms and nothing else -- its members are the predicates the equivalence cannot see past and its closure is saturation along it -- so the frame is a function of a setoid, and invariance of the semantics read in it needs only that the step relation respects that setoid. Both frames this tree uses are that construction, on the nose and provably, and the disciplined frame's invariance theorem, its closure under the semantics, and its predicate-valued formula interpretation are instantiations of the generic ones rather than second proofs. The collapse the permissive theory suffers is then stated at full strength: the identification is not special to the terminated process, because the reverse direction of the reflection equation matches a bare schema variable, so every pattern whatsoever is equated with the name that quotes its drop. A predicate of the form is a quote up to the equations therefore holds of everything in that theory, which is exactly what the tree's generated-logic bound on the source's scope generator says -- true, and empty. The same bound read in the disciplined frame has content and refutes membership: the terminated process is not in the disciplined reading of the source's scope, whatever the two part predicates are. That is the negative this development had been proving in the ambient powerset for want of anywhere better to put it, and it now lives in the frame the positives live in. What is not written and not claimed: the discipline is stated for authored instances only, since the derived laws already carry their own sorting judgement; and the canonical OSLF entry points still read the permissive theory, so a presentation opts into the discipline by naming the disciplined frame rather than by a change of default." }
  , { area := "Equation Semantics"
      title := "Admissible equations: lean representatives, a hereditary measure, and a sort that does not move"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/StructuralModal/AdmissibleEquations.lean: Admissible / Admissible.leanInduction / Admissible.sepConj_at_lean / Admissible.sepConj_sort / Admissible.measure_lt_of_lean_singleton / UnitPadding.unit / UnitPadding.IsAtom / UnitPadding.Carrier / UnitPadding.Equiv / UnitPadding.equiv_refl / UnitPadding.equiv_symm / UnitPadding.equiv_trans / UnitPadding.IsLean / UnitPadding.measure / UnitPadding.sortedAt / UnitPadding.carrier_of_filter_eq / UnitPadding.admissible / UnitPadding.padded_carrier / UnitPadding.padded_not_lean / UnitPadding.padded_representative / UnitPadding.measure_decreases"
      note := "The separating conjunction quantifies over decompositions rather than recursing through them, so it says what a split is without saying how to find one. A procedure that searched for a split would descend -- pick a representative, break it into parts, repeat on the parts -- and the source material's three conditions on an equation theory are exactly what makes that terminate. They are now stated and each is proved to do its job. Every class has a lean representative, so the descent has somewhere to start and starts on a term that carries the parts it appears to carry rather than padding; leanness is hereditary with a strictly decreasing measure, so the parts of a lean composition are themselves lean and smaller; and the theory relates only terms of the same sort, so a change of representative cannot leave the sort the descent works in. The conditions are asked of a carrier rather than of every pattern, because an equation theory is a theory of a presentation's terms and a representative outside the carrier is something no presentation supplies. What they buy is proved: the descent's induction principle, that every split of a carrier term is a split of a lean representative so the search can move there without losing it, and that a split never crosses a sort. The measure's condition is shown to have content rather than being carried -- in any admissible theory a lean one-element composition is strictly larger than its element, so a theory with a constant measure has no lean one-element compositions at all. A presentation meeting all three is given: compositions of atoms with one law, that a unit part may be dropped, with leanness meaning carrying no unit and the measure counting parts. Its equivalence is proved reflexive, symmetric and transitive, and all three conditions are discharged. The witnesses show none of them is vacuous there: a padded composition is a term of the carrier and is not lean, its lean representative is a different term, and the measure strictly decreases into the parts of a lean composition of two atoms. What is not written and not claimed: a decision procedure for the connective is not built. The three conditions are what such a procedure would consume and each is proved to do its job, but turning them into a procedure needs one more thing -- that a split of a lean representative is recoverable from a split of its element list -- which is a property of a particular equation theory rather than of admissibility, and is not supplied here." }
  , { area := "Context-Decorated Logic"
      title := "Context-labelled congruence relative to a class, and box through least enablers"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/AdmissibleContextCongruence.lean: AdmissibleClass / AdmissibleClass.labelledSystem / LeastEnablerComposes / ObservationsRespectClass / bisimilar_plug_labelled / labelsAdmissible_forces_total / NecessityCanaries.congruence_fails_labelled / NecessityCanaries.identityOnly / NecessityCanaries.identityOnly_proper / NecessityCanaries.identityOnly_congruence / NecessityCanaries.observations_do_not_respect_class; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/LeastEnablerBox.lean: backwardSystem / box / dia / box_eq_not_dia_not / BackwardImageFiniteModulo / backward_logicallyEquivalent_iff_bisimilar; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/AdmissibleContexts.lean: QuoteFreePath / quoteFreePath_append / quoting_context_separates; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/RelativePushout.lean: Candidate / Candidate.self / Candidate.Mediates / Candidate.Refines / Candidate.mediates_comp / IsRelativePushout / IsIdemPushout / IsRelativePushout.refines / IsIdemPushout.down_splits / IsRelativePushout.unique / isIdemPushout_of_isPushout / isIdemPushout_of_isRelativePushout / HasRelativePushouts / exists_idemPushout_below / idemPushout_below_factors / isRelativePushout_self_of_isIdemPushout / isRelativePushout_postcompose / isIdemPushout_paste / isIdemPushout_residual / overSpanLeft / overSpanRight / overInl / overInr / sliceCandidate / overSq / isPushout_over_iff_isIdemPushout; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/IPOSystem.lean: ReactionRule / ActIPO / IsIPOBisimulation / IPOBisimilar; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/RedexRelativeCongruence.lean: ipoBisimilar_forward / ipoBisimilar_backward / AgentJudgment / ContextRules / actIPO_context_replay / contextRules_locally_respectful / ipoBisimilar_comp; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/RedexRelativeEnabling.lean: twoChannel_hasRelativePushouts / twoChannel_every_bound_reduces / isIdemPushout_tok / outer_isIdemPushout / paste_instance / paste_instance_enlarges / cutCandidate / min_eq_zero_of_isIdemPushout / isIdemPushout_tok_iff / Congruence.hasRelativePushouts_all / Congruence.congruence / Congruence.pairRule / Congruence.oneRule / Congruence.token_steps / Congruence.act_token_iff / Congruence.distinct_bisimilar / Congruence.distinct_agents / Congruence.congruence_instance / twoChannelGSLT / twoChannelRules / completeFirst_enables / completeSecond_enables / completeFirst_not_factors / completeSecond_not_factors / no_least_enabler / no_act / source_reduces_first / source_reduces_second / tok / tok_comp / tok_injective / tok_surjective / squareFirst / squareSecond / first_isIdemPushout / second_isIdemPushout / two_relative_minima_no_absolute_minimum; Mettapedia/GSLT/Logic/BagRelativePushout.lean: Bag / Obj / bag / bag_comp / bag_id / bag_injective / bag_surjective / cutCandidate / hasRelativePushouts / isIdemPushout_bag / congruence; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformLabels.lean: receiverTerm / outputA / outputB / firedTerm / redexParts / reactumParts / asProcess / reaction_realised / reaction_realised_in_context / redexBag / reactumBag / agentBag / labelBag / joinReaction / platformRules / platform_hasRelativePushouts / platform_congruence / platform_act"
      note := "The admissible context class is a parameter that does work rather than decorating, and congruence is proved from exactly two named properties: least enablers composing with the class, and observations not looking through it. The labels of the system are the admissible contexts, so a label is admissible by construction and the composed label of a step out of a filled context is admissible by the class being closed under composition; that is where the closure condition earns its place. Labelling with every context of the theory instead and then asking as a hypothesis that every label be admissible forces the class to be everything, which is now itself a theorem so that the defect cannot quietly return. The difference is exhibited on one theory: with the class cut to the identity context congruence holds, and with the class left unrestricted it fails, the two statements differing only in the class. A theory with no rules witnesses that the second cannot be dropped. Box is defined over labelled predecessors in the reversed least-enabler system, so backward adequacy is the forward theorem applied to it and needs only image-finiteness modulo the equations, not finiteness of raw predecessors. For rho the class is the quote-free positions, closed under composition; two inert processes separated by one quoting context witness that excluding holes under a quote is necessary. The obstruction to a rho instance is now located, and it is not a missing proof. The least-enabler property asks a context to factor into every context that enables the rule, and a source completable in two incomparable ways has no such context at all: a theory with two channels is exhibited where one token on the first channel is completed either by a second token there or by a self-contained pair on the other, neither completion factors through the other, and a least enabler would therefore have to be the empty context, which does not enable. So the labelled relation has no transition out of that term, though the term reduces in context two different ways. That is the shape of a reflective calculus, and it is why the composition law was never discharged. The universal property that does hold is redex-relative, and it is the relative pushout: a bound closing the source against a chosen redex, least among the bounds it factors through. That notion is formalised for an arbitrary category, proved to be exactly a pushout in the slice over the bound's apex -- so it is the ordinary universal property read where the bound lives, not a new one beside it -- and a pushout is shown to be one of them. In the canary the contexts compose by addition, so they are the morphisms of a one-object category and terms are morphisms of the same category; both completions are then proved to be idem pushouts there, one for each redex. Two least labels where the absolute notion had none. Existence is now met rather than carried. A relative pushout's own bound is proved to be an idem pushout, so taking the relative pushout of a bound produces one that wastes nothing; a span has relative pushouts when every bound on it has one; and the two together give that every bound reduces to an idem pushout, with the reduction a genuine factorisation of the original bound. The canary satisfies the existence condition for every span and every bound, by the obvious construction -- the largest part two bounds share is their componentwise minimum, and cutting it away is least -- so a theory with least labels for every reaction it can perform is exhibited rather than hypothesised. Pasting is proved. An idem pushout post-composed with a further context is the relative pushout of the enlarged bound -- the retract argument, using relative-pushout existence -- and from that, two squares paste: if the inner square is least for its redex at a term and the outer square is least for the inner label, the composite is least for that redex at the term in the enlarged context. That is the property a context-labelled transition relation needs in place of the composition law that cannot hold. It is instantiated non-degenerately: in the canary a bound is least exactly when its two legs share nothing, which is proved once and turns the question into arithmetic, and enlarging the source by an inert token on the other channel is shown not to move the label. The congruence is now proved over redex-relative labels, and it holds for every context with no class of admissible contexts at all -- the class parameter was the price of a transition relation that demanded a label least among every enabling context, which fails in the exhibited two-channel theory. Three two-square lemmas carry it: an idem pushout post-composed with a further context is the relative pushout of the enlarged bound, two squares paste, and the residual square of a relative pushout is itself least. The labelled transition admits a firing only with the leastness, so a step out of a filled context presents a bound at the filling, relative pushouts reduce it, bisimilarity matches the reduced step, and pasting puts the context back carrying the original label. None of it is assumed where it could be met. Existence of relative pushouts is discharged for the canary at every span; leastness there is characterised exactly, in both directions, as the two legs of a bound sharing nothing; the labelled transition relation is inhabited; and the congruence is instantiated at two distinct agents that are bisimilar, not at reflexivity. The rho platform receives the instance. Its contexts are parallel remainders, so its context category is the one-object category on bags of processes, and that category is proved to have relative pushouts for every span and every bound -- the part two bounds share is their bag intersection, and cutting it away is least. A bound whose legs share nothing is least, which is the criterion in the form a calculus uses. So the congruence holds on the platform for every context with nothing assumed, and the class the deliverable asks for -- contexts excluding holes under quote -- is the whole context category, because a bag places processes beside the hole and cannot put it under a quote. The reaction rule is the presentation's own rather than invented: the engine is checked in the kernel to compute exactly the reactum from the redex, first alone and then beside a process the rule must leave alone. The labelled transition relation is inhabited at that rule. The congruence theorem now runs in an arbitrary category with a fixed origin: agents have interface-indexed codomains, labels and contexts are composable arrows, and bisimulation is a family over interfaces. Behavioral classes form a genuine functor on that context category, with identity and composition proved from the congruence rather than by choosing representatives. Controls show a Bool-to-Option-Bool labelled transition and reject a shared nonleast context; the token instance identifies distinct agents while retaining distinct classes and exhibits a context that changes a class. The rho instantiation remains the bag context category. HigherOrderBisimulation constructs positional label comparison: skeletons agree literally, while corresponding payloads and successors use one monotone greatest fixed point over interface-indexed states. Its behavioral classes and quotient steps are proved, and literal matching on the resulting label classes recovers that same bisimilarity. Nested-payload and Bool/Nat two-slot controls retain observable distinctions; empty payloads recover the existing IPO relation. This does not supply an executable class-computation algorithm or transfer the literal-label congruence theorem: behaviorally related inner labels require a relation-respecting residual/pasting argument, and observations must respect the chosen context class. What is not constructed: a context category for every authored language definition together with its RPO-existence proof, congruence for all rho prefixes and payload contexts, or a source-derived higher-order label decomposition together with its binding/substitution and contextual-congruence laws." }
