      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/RedexPosition.lean: subtermAt / plug / plug_subtermAt / relyVars / hiddenVars / slotCount / fvarNames_eq; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedHypercubeInstances.lean: rhoCommPaper / rhoCommPaper_is_rhoComm_without_rest / rhoCommPaper_relyVars / rhoCommPaper_slotCount / rhoCommPaper_relyVars_declared / rhoCommPaperCenter / rhoCommPaper_center_card / rhoCommPaper_center_eq_univ / rhoCommPaperSquare / rhoCommPaper_square_card / rhoCommPaper_square_is_face / rhoComm_square_needs_two_conditions; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedHypercube.lean: evalSort / derivedAdmissible / derivedPresentation / derivedCenter; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedModality.lean: StablePath / subtermAt_applyBindings / plug_applyBindings / RelyPossibly / relyPossibly_congr_relyVars / relyPossibly_intro / relyPossibly_step / relyPossibly_elim; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedHypercubeInstances.lean; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedModalityRho.lean; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/RelyPossiblyTypeFormer.lean: relyPossiblyType / relyPossiblyType_spec / relyPossiblyType_of_relyPossibly / relyPossibly_of_relyPossiblyType / relyPossiblyType_congr_relyVars / relyPossiblyType_intro / relyPossiblyType_step / relyPossiblyType_elim / satisfies_relyPossiblyType ; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedModality.lean: relyPossibly_step_authored / relyPossibly_mono_result / not_relyPossibly_of_result_empty / rhsOnlyRelyPossibly / rhsOnlyRelyPossibly_result_independent_of_term / relyPossibly_of_rhsOnly ; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/RelyPossiblyTypeFormer.lean: relyPossibly_invariant_of_equationFree / relyPossiblyType_iff_relyPossibly_of_equationFree / relyPossiblyType_step_of_equationFree / relyPossiblyType_elim_of_equationFree / Discharged.vec_invariant / Discharged.vec_type_iff_raw / Discharged.bag_outside_class ; Mettapedia/GSLT/Meredith/Modal/RewriteModality.lean: ModalFormation.sortAssignment_eq / not_modalFormation_of_outputSort_ne / RelyPossibly / relyPossibly_intro / relyPossibly_step / relyPossibly_elim / relyPossibly_mono / not_relyPossibly_of_post_empty / rhsOnlyReading / rhsOnlyReading_independent_of_term / rhsOnlyReading_subterm_iff; Mettapedia/OSLF/Framework/GeneratedModalFamily.lean: Site / redexSites / mem_redexSites_iff / root_site_mem / siteRelyVars / siteSlotCount / siteSlotCount_eq / siteCenter / siteCenter_eq / siteFace / siteModality / siteModality_eq / allRelyVarsDeclared / relyVarsDeclared_of_all / exists_undeclared_of_not_all; Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/PlatformModalFamily.lean: rhoCalc_site_count / rhoCalc_fails_check / rhoCalc_undeclared_count / rhoCalc_has_undeclared_site / platform_site_count / platform_passes_check / platform_every_site_declared / check_separates_presentations / joinSite / joinSite_one_mem / joinSite_two_mem / joinSite_one_slotCount / joinSite_one_center_eq_univ / joinSite_one_face_card / joinSite_one_face_is_face / joinSite_two_slotCount / joinSite_two_center_card / joinSite_two_face_card / cube_dimension_tracks_arity"
      note := "The declared-rule analysis enumerates every left-hand-side position and computes its rely names, slots, declaration checks, cube coordinates, and raw rely-possibly predicate. The introduction, step, and elimination laws remain valid at their advertised relational types and under their stated decomposition/step hypotheses; they do not construct the source generated typing judgments. The native former is equation saturation, with raw-reading recovery and elimination requiring equation-invariance, discharged only for the explicit equation-free class. The center evaluator admits unsupported analysis branches as true and does not establish sorting, reduction congruence, or the source universal property. Cube cardinalities and hand-contrasted faces therefore do not discharge the worked source example: the source fixes the channel, whereas these fixtures fix the output. The platform family exercises declared arity and distinguishes an undeclared collection rest, but its ground/parallel reaction scope is not the full reflective calculus. A free compatible extension, its adjunction/monad and morphism action, and source-faithful center/type-former generation remain open." }
  , { area := "OSLF Core **The rely-possibly modality is defined three times in this repository, on three carriers, and the three are now related by a single scheme.**  GSLT/Meredith/Modal/RewriteModality.lean defines it over a lambda theory as an existential over reducts; OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean defines it over intrinsically scoped closed terms as a universal over rely environments yielding a rule instance; OSLF/Framework/GeneratedModality.lean defines it over untyped patterns as a universal over bindings guarded by rule firing.  OSLF/Framework/RelyPossiblyScheme.lean supplies the missing agreement.  A RelyFrame carries five components -- what the modality is a predicate on, what indexes it, what its existential ranges over, when a witness fits an index, and what a witness produces -- and its modality is `forall e, rely e -> exists w, Fit w e t and B (out w)`.  Each of the three definitions is that scheme at its own choice of components: categorical_is_instance, pattern_is_instance and scoped_is_instance are the bridges, each an Iff against the existing definition and none of them rfl, since the three differ from the scheme by collapsing a quantifier over Unit, by currying two hypotheses, and by re-associating a conjunction respectively.  **What the identification buys.**  modality_iff_diamond reads the modality as a meet, over the admissible environments, of the relational diamonds of the induced step relations, and diamond_adjunction proves the diamond is the left adjoint of substitution along that relation.  Monotonicity in the target, antitonicity in the rely assumptions, splitting of a disjunctive rely condition, vacuity under an empty rely condition, and refutation by an empty target are then proved once at the scheme.  Each carrier's own published laws are re-derived from them with their statements copied unchanged, as compiler-checked example blocks beside each bridge, so the claim that the abstraction suffices is checked rather than asserted.  **Why the lambda-theory presentation looked incompatible.**  It is the rely-free instance: its environment type is Unit, so its universal quantifier collapses and only the existential is visible.  That is a choice of index, not a different construction.  **What the identification does not buy, stated as theorems.**  The three are instances of one scheme; they are not interchangeable.  At a trivial index the modality is a single diamond and therefore preserves joins of targets (categorical_preserves_joins); at a genuine index it provably does not (join_not_preserved exhibits a frame, a term and two targets where the modality holds of their disjunction and of neither disjunct).  And with an inhabited environment type but no admissible environment the modality holds of everything whatever the target (modality_of_no_admissible, target_need_not_be_load_bearing) -- a situation the rely-free instance cannot be in, since its index is inhabited and its rely condition is True.  So a result proved at one carrier transports to another only along a map of frames, and no such map is built here.  **The remaining step, now expressible.**  FrameMorphism is the map of frames -- covariant in carriers, outputs and witnesses, contravariant in the index -- and FrameMorphism.modality_map transports the modality along one; transport_is_directed shows it runs one way only, by exhibiting a map whose target satisfies a modality its source refutes.  A morphism from scopedFrame to patternFrame would therefore carry results between the two rely-indexed carriers, and the structure now says exactly what such a morphism is: a function on patterns, a function from binding lists back to rely environments, a function from rule instances to decomposition-and-step pairs, and proofs that fitting and production are preserved.  OSLF/Syntax/PatternAsBindingSignature.lean already maps intrinsically scoped terms to patterns by erasure with the substitution and plugging correspondences proved, which is the raw material for its action on witnesses.  What is missing is that erasure carries a rule instance to a binding list and that the scoped step corresponds to rule firing.  Until that exists, the two rely-indexed carriers agree in shape and not in content."
      title := "LanguageDef → GSLT modulo equations → OSLF pipeline"
