      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: embed / embedArgs / argsToSub / instantiate / instantiateArgs / instantiate_embed / instantiateArgs_embedArgs / RuleInstance / RootStep / rootStep_of_instance / rootStep_lhs_shape / rootStep_rhs_shape; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.contDiscard / RhoSchema.contUnquote / RhoSchema.rhs_under_discard / RhoSchema.rhs_under_unquote / RhoSchema.instantiations_differ / RhoSchema.nilP / RhoSchema.chan / RhoSchema.closeComm / RhoSchema.commInstance / RhoSchema.instance_source / RhoSchema.instance_target / RhoSchema.rho_communicates / RhoSchema.nil_does_not_step"
      note := "A schema becomes a rule by supplying a body for each metavariable. Because metavariables were adjoined as operators, that operation is the signature morphism replacing them, and applying a body to the arguments the schema handed it is the term algebra's own substitution - so no second mechanism is introduced and the round trip through the base signature is the identity. A rule instance is then a body for each metavariable together with closed terms for the rule's own variables, and the two roles are genuinely different: the metavariables are what the rule is parametric in, while the context variables are the ones a redex position can be taken at, because a hole has to be pluggable. The root-level relation a positioned rewrite denotes is defined from that, and it doubles as the specification any matcher must meet, since a matcher is correct exactly when the assignment it returns satisfies it. Two shape lemmas invert a step back to its instance, which is what lets a concrete rule's head be read off. On the reflective calculus the rule fires: with the channel closed to the quote of the null process and the continuation instantiated to unquote what it receives, the rule carries the source to the reflective round trip on the received name, and that target is produced by the rule rather than written down. Instance and control are both present - two different continuations give two different right-hand sides, so the rule is a schema and not one reaction, and the null process does not step, because a rule headed by parallel composition can only fire on a term headed by parallel composition. Not yet built: an executable matcher meeting this specification, and the contextual closure that lets the rule fire below the root."
    }
  , { area := "Generated Type Systems"
      title := "Firing below the root, and the rely-indexed modality generated at a chosen position"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: Step / inst_hole / holeCount_hole / step_of_rootStep / unconditioned_closure_is_reflexive / StepsFromPosition / stepsFromPosition_intro / stepsFromPosition_step / stepsFromPosition_elim / stepsFromPosition_mono / Poss / poss_mono / Separated / local_of_not_rely / not_separated_of_shared / RelyTyping / AgreesOnRely / RelyEnv / Realises / relyEnvOf / realises_relyEnvOf / agreesOnRely_iff_realises / RelyPossibly / relyPossibly_intro / relyPossibly_step / relyPossibly_elim / relyPossibly_mono_target / relyPossibly_mono_rely / stepsFromPosition_of_relyPossibly; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.commSource / RhoSchema.commTarget / RhoSchema.parContext / RhoSchema.parContext_linear / RhoSchema.rho_communicates_in_context / RhoSchema.nil_does_not_step_in_context / RhoSchema.payload_steps / RhoSchema.payload_does_not_step_into_nothing / RhoSchema.comm_separated / RhoSchema.closeWith / RhoSchema.payload_rely_possibly / RhoSchema.payload_rely_possibly_needs_target / RhoSchema.payload_steps_at_every_channel"
      note := "The contextual closure fires a rule inside a one-hole context, and the context is required to use its hole. That requirement is not decoration: drop it and a context that ignores its hole relates every term to itself whenever the rule fires anywhere at all, which is proved rather than asserted. So the occurrence condition introduced for redex positions does a second, independent job here, which is the evidence that it was the right abstraction rather than a patch. On the reflective calculus the communication fires under a parallel remainder, and the null process does not step even below the root: either the context is the bare hole, and then the null process would have to step at the root, which it does not, or the context is headed by an operator, and matching the null process forces that operator to be the null former, whose only context has no hole. That inversion became possible only after operators were indexed by the sort they produce; before that a term's sort was a stuck function application and no eliminator could invert it, which blocked every inversion lemma and therefore any matcher. Indexing also retired the separate result field, so the signature carries two fields where it carried three. Above the step relation sits the possibility generated at a chosen position: the rule's own instances supply the step, the construction is indexed by the rule and its position, and introduction, the delivery of an operational step rather than a conversion, its transport into the contextual closure, and monotonicity in the target predicate are all proved. Above that sits the modality itself, with its rely parameter indexed. Its quantifier structure is the source's rely-possibly reading and is therefore mixed: universal over environments meeting the typed assumptions, existential over everything the rule still gets to choose, with the chosen instance required to agree with the environment wherever the rule relies. Introduction, delivery of an operational step rather than a conversion, transport into the contextual closure, monotonicity in the target predicate and antitonicity in the assumptions are proved, together with the refinement back to the unindexed possibility. Indexing the rely parameters needs the rely and local families to partition the rule's variables, which they do not do in general, since a variable occurring in both the context and the redex belongs to neither. That condition is named, its failure is characterised by exhibiting such a shared variable, and the communication rule is proved to satisfy it - the channel relies, the payload is local. On that rule the modality is inhabited at every channel the environment may supply, which is what relying on a parameter means, with two controls: the target predicate is genuinely consulted, so neither the possibility nor the modality is vacuously inhabited."
    }
  , { area := "Generated Type Systems"
      title := "The structural layer, the propositional layer finite limits supply, and the separating conjunction the equations supply"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: Pred / PredArgs / SatArgs / structural / structural_intro / structural_elim / structural_not_var / structural_head_unique / PredTop / PredAnd / predTop_intro / predAnd_intro / predAnd_left / predAnd_right; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.dropChan / RhoSchema.isNil / RhoSchema.isDropChan / RhoSchema.isChan / RhoSchema.par_structural / RhoSchema.nil_not_par_structural / RhoSchema.boundIsDropped / RhoSchema.inp_structural / RhoSchema.par_structural_is_positional / RhoSchema.parT / RhoSchema.SepAnd / RhoSchema.sepAnd_comm / RhoSchema.sepAnd_of_structural"
      note := "One type former is generated per term former, indexed by the signature's operators rather than written per calculus, and each former's argument slots are indexed by that operator's binding arity. The consequence worth stating is that a binding argument carries a predicate at the context it opens, not at the ambient one, so the layer reaches binder positions instead of stopping at them: the input former's continuation slot is inhabited by a predicate about the received name, and that instance is exhibited rather than described. Introduction and elimination are proved, a variable inhabits no structural type, and terms cannot inhabit the types of two different heads, so the layer classifies rather than overlaps. The propositional layer is stratified by what the base actually supplies: finite limits give a terminal object and pullbacks, hence top and conjunction with their introductions and projections, and nothing further is added, since disjunction, falsity and implication would be claiming structure finite limits do not provide. Two controls: the null process does not inhabit the parallel type, so the layer reads the head; and swapping the two sides of a parallel type leaves it uninhabited. That second one is the point of the row. What a free signature supplies at an interaction former is a *positional* split, proved positional rather than glossed as a separating conjunction; the separating reading needs the former's associativity and commutativity, which live in the equations. With those now available the separating conjunction is built on top of the structural type - a process is in it when it is equationally a parallel composition of a part in each argument's predicate - and it is proved commutative, which the positional split is proved not to be. The structural type refines into it, so the two layers are related rather than parallel."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "Equations on the binding-signature carrier, and stepping modulo them"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: EqAxiom / EqClosure / EqArgs / eqArgs_refl / StepModE / stepModE_of_step / stepModE_resp_left / stepModE_resp_right; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.commPar / RhoSchema.assocPar / RhoSchema.rhoE / RhoSchema.closePair / RhoSchema.par_comm"
      note := "The third component of a language definition, on the carrier where binding is declared by the signature. An axiom is two sides of one sort in one variable context, possibly mentioning metavariables; the theory it generates is the least equivalence containing the axioms' instances and closed under the term formers. Closure under the formers is stated once, argument by argument, rather than once per operator, and because each argument is related at the context its binding arity opens, the closure passes under binders instead of stopping at them. Stepping modulo the equations is then the relation a presentation with equations actually denotes, and it respects the theory on both sides, with an ordinary step being a step modulo. The same construction already exists on the older pattern carrier in the language-definition layer, with authored equation instances, a context closure, the equivalence closure, and a step relation modulo it carrying the same two respect lemmas; this is not a new idea but the same one on a carrier with explicitly binder-preserving substitution and where the closure under formers needs no per-constructor case. On the reflective calculus the interaction former's associativity and commutativity are authored as axioms and commutativity is derived for arbitrary processes, which is what the separating conjunction in the structural row rests on."
