  , { area := "Generated Type Systems"
      title := "Sort slots, the equational center, the hypercube, and positions whose hole carries a binding arity"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: Slot / Filling / SlotLaws / Center / origin / origin_mem_center / center_of_no_laws / center_ne_univ_of_identification / Cube / card_cube / card_axes / card_cube_three / card_axes_three / card_square / square_is_two_slot_cube / soleBody / AbstractionPosition / AbstractionPosition.carrier / AbstractionPosition.RelyParameter / AbstractionPosition.Slot; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.chanSlot / RhoSchema.outSlot / RhoSchema.chanSlot_ne_outSlot / RhoSchema.payload_has_no_slot / RhoSchema.holeArity / RhoSchema.holeSig / RhoSchema.holeAt / RhoSchema.contCtxt / RhoSchema.contRedex / RhoSchema.contLhs / RhoSchema.continuationPosition / RhoSchema.chan_rely / RhoSchema.payload_rely / RhoSchema.slotN / RhoSchema.slotP / RhoSchema.slotOut / RhoSchema.slotN_ne_out / RhoSchema.slotP_ne_out / RhoSchema.slotN_ne_slotP"
      note := "Each generated type former carries finitely many sort slots - one per rely input and one for the output - and the slots are read off the rule rather than postulated, which the definition records by indexing a slot by a rely parameter together with the proof that it is one. Filling each slot two ways gives a raw cube; the identifications that equations and rewrite laws force between slots cut it down to the assignments stable under them, and those are the hypercube's vertices. Both halves of that are proved rather than described: with no identifications the center is the whole raw cube, which is why the Lambda Cube never needs the distinction, and as soon as two distinct slots are identified some filling is excluded, so the center is a proper part whenever a presentation carries equations. The counting is general - a raw cube on n slots has two-to-the-n vertices and two-to-the-n minus one local axes relative to the origin - and the worked example's arithmetic is checked against it: three slots give eight vertices and seven axes, and holding one slot at the origin leaves four, which is exactly the cube on the remaining two slots. On the communication rule the slots are exhibited: the channel is a rely input and gets one, the output gets one, they are distinct, and the payload gets none because it is local, so the slot count is a fact about the chosen position rather than about how many variables the rule has. The worked example's own position is then built rather than approximated. It selects an abstraction, not a term, which is why the source gives that position an exponential carrier and why its classifying theory must be cartesian closed. A hole that binds is a metavariable, so plugging is metavariable instantiation, which already exists: the position needs no new machinery and the object language needs no function sorts. Building it recovers the source's rely set exactly - the channel and the emitted process are both rely inputs - so the modality carries three slots, and those three are exhibited and proved pairwise distinct rather than counted. One consequence is structural. The redex of such a position is open only in what the hole binds and cannot mention the ambient variables, because its type forbids it, so the subtraction the source performs has nothing to subtract and the failure recorded for variable-holes - a variable in both families belonging to neither - cannot arise at an abstraction position at all."
    }
  , { area := "Generated Type Systems"
      title := "Adjoining and forgetting: how the original theory sits inside its free extension"
      status := .inProgress
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: usesMeta_embed / usesMetaArgs_embedArgs / exists_embed_of_not_usesMeta / exists_embedArgs_of_not_usesMetaArgs / embed_injective / instantiate_embed / instantiateArgs_embedArgs / idArgs / metaVar / instInto / instIntoArgs / argsToSub_renameArgs / argsToSub_idArgs / instInto_rename / instIntoArgs_renameArgs / instIntoArgs_idArgs / instInto_metaVar / bindArgs_argsToSub_idArgs / instInto_metaVar_id / instIntoArgs_metaVar_id / argsToSub_bindArgs / argsToSub_instIntoArgs / instInto_liftSub / instInto_bind / instIntoArgs_bindArgs / instInto_instInto / instIntoArgs_instIntoArgs / instInto_extend / instInto_inst; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.discardMetas / RhoSchema.metaHoleCtxt / RhoSchema.metaHoleCtxt_linear / RhoSchema.discardBody / RhoSchema.instInto_discard_erases / RhoSchema.instInto_destroys_position"
      note := "The source states the construction as a free-forgetful resolution: a forgetful functor from theories carrying the generated layers to theories, a left adjoint freely adjoining them, and the induced endofunctor a monad whose value at a theory is the underlying theory of its free extension. What is proved here is the part of that statement about how a theory sits inside its free extension, on the signature layer where the extension is concretely adjoining operators. The inclusion lands in the metavariable-free part, and conversely every metavariable-free term of the extension is in the image, so the image is exactly that part rather than merely contained in it. The inclusion is injective, because supplying any bodies at all recovers the term, and reading a term of the extension back down by supplying bodies is a retraction of the inclusion, which is one of the two triangle identities in concrete form. The multiplication is now built, and it needed no notion of signature morphism after all. Reading a term of an extension back down by supplying bodies lands in the base signature, so it cannot be iterated; letting the bodies themselves carry metavariables gives the operation that can be, taking a term over one extension to a term over another. Its unit is a metavariable applied to its own variables, and the left unit law is proved: instantiating at the unit returns the body supplied. Proving it required generalising the lifting of renamings so that it does not mention the operators at all, only the sorts - the same correction already made for variables, and for the same reason, that the two sides of an equation were elaborating the operation at different signatures. The right unit law is proved too: instantiating every metavariable by itself is the identity, which rests on the lemma that substituting a metavariable's own variables by the reading of its arguments returns those arguments. Associativity is proved as well, so the construction is a monad: instantiating twice is instantiating once along the composite. It rests on instantiation commuting with substitution, which rests on it commuting with the lifting of a substitution past binders, and on two lemmas saying that reading a substitution off arguments commutes with substituting or instantiating those arguments. The transport the source displays for the action on morphisms is then examined for the morphism that actually arises here, which is instantiation. Plugging transports: instantiating a one-hole context and its redex separately and then plugging gives the instantiation of the plugged term. But the action on *positions* is partial, and that is exhibited rather than assumed. A supplied body which discards its argument erases the hole, so a context using its hole exactly once is carried to one that does not use it at all, and the transported decomposition is no longer a position. Carrying a position along an instantiation therefore needs the supplied bodies to use the argument that carries the hole, and that condition is not automatic. The transport formula as the source writes it presumes the transported context is still a one-hole context; on this reading it is not in general. What remains unbuilt is the same formula for morphisms that change the signature, which needs a notion of signature morphism this development does not carry."
    }
  , { area := "Generated Type Systems"
      title := "The three dials: language fragment, connective fragment, cube vertex"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: LanguageFragment / InFragment / InFragmentArgs / fullFragment / emptyFragment / inFragment_mono / inFragmentArgs_mono / not_inFragment_empty / inFragment_var / ConnectiveFragment / fullConnectives / conjunctiveModal / conjunctiveModal_ne_full / Dials / dials_independent; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.nameFree / RhoSchema.par_nils_nameFree / RhoSchema.dropChan_not_nameFree / RhoSchema.nameFree_lt_full"
      note := "The generated logic is fixed by a language specification together with a choice of connectives, so a user selects fragments to trade expressivity for checkability along three axes. The first is the sub-signature properties may be stated over: a term lies in a fragment when every head it uses does, widening a fragment admits more terms, variables are in every fragment including the empty one, and the empty fragment admits no constructed term at all - so the trade is real rather than nominal. The second is which generated connectives are in play, recorded as flags for the top predicate, conjunction, the structural layer, the modality and the possibility. There is deliberately no flag for implication or negation: the propositional layer is stratified by what the classifying theory supplies, and finite limits supply conjunction and the top predicate only, so a flag for the others would be offering structure the base does not provide. The third is a vertex of the hypercube, which is an element of the equational center built in the row above. The three are independent, and that is stated as a theorem rather than asserted: fixing the language and the connectives leaves configurations that differ at the vertex. On the reflective calculus the first dial is instantiated at the name-free fragment - no quoting and no dropping, hence no reflection - with a process inside it, a process outside it that unquotes, and a proof that the fragment is a proper restriction of the whole signature."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "Decidable equality of terms, and a sound first-order matcher on the binding-signature carrier"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: decEqVar / decEqTerm / decEqArgs / PSub / emptyPSub / updatePSub / updatePSub_self / updatePSub_mono / matchT / matchA / PExtends / matchT_mono / matchA_mono / matchT_sound / matchA_sound / reScope / weakenInto / liftSub_reScope / bind_weakenInto; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/RhoCommunicationSchema.lean: RhoSchema.opDecEq / RhoSchema.outPattern / RhoSchema.outTarget / RhoSchema.outPattern_matches / RhoSchema.outPattern_does_not_match_nil / RhoSchema.outPattern_match_sound / RhoSchema.commTargetExpl / RhoSchema.commLhs_matches / RhoSchema.commLhs_does_not_match_nil"
      note := "Equality of terms is decided, which nothing on this carrier could do before and which any matcher needs, since a pattern mentioning the same variable twice matches only when both positions carry equal subterms. The delicate case is the operator one - two terms of one sort may be headed by different operators whose argument lists then have different types - and it is handled by settling the operators first so the lists become comparable, rather than by transporting one along an equality. The matcher itself is first order: it takes a pattern whose free variables are the rule's and a closed term, and returns the bindings, descending into non-binding arguments and stopping at binding ones, since a binding slot's body lives under binders the closed term does not share and belongs to the metavariable layer instead. The matcher threads a partial substitution rather than collecting bindings and concatenating them. That is not a style choice, and the reason is a defect the proof found in the first attempt: with concatenation a binding from an earlier sibling shadows a later one, so a substitution agreeing with the concatenated result need not agree with each part, and soundness of the recursion does not follow from agreement. Threading removes the possibility, since a variable already bound is checked against its existing value rather than re-bound, and the consistency check the first design needed is then unnecessary rather than unproved. Monotonicity and soundness are both proved by mutual induction: matching only ever adds bindings, and any closing substitution realising the result carries the pattern to the target. A binding argument is not descended into, since its body lives under binders the closed term does not share; that slot belongs to the metavariable layer, and the restriction is in the type rather than assumed. A binding argument is handled by comparing the pattern's body against the target's body seen in the opened scope, which is a renaming rather than a substitution, and the obligation that falls out - a body which is merely the target's is carried back to it by any closing substitution - is proved by showing that lifting a closing substitution leaves the bound prefix alone. That keeps the first-order layer honest about what it can match: a binding slot whose body genuinely depends on the rule's variables belongs to the metavariable layer, and only a slot whose body is the target's is accepted here. On the reflective calculus the output pattern is matched against a closed output, a target with a different head is refused, the general soundness theorem is instantiated at that pattern, and the communication rule's own left-hand side, with its continuation supplied, matches the closed source through the input former's binding argument."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "The executable reflective model's substitution captures, and the presentation that repairs it"
      status := .inProgress
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/Languages/ProcessCalculi/RhoCalculus/SubstitutionCaptureCanary.lean: capturedBody / receiverBindingOne / receiverBindingTwo / capturingSubst / substProc_captures / substProc_alpha_variant / delivery_after_capture / delivery_after_alpha_variant / alpha_variants_diverge; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/ProcAsBindingSignature.lean: ProcMigration.PSrt / ProcMigration.POp / ProcMigration.psig / ProcMigration.ctxOf / ProcMigration.lookupEnv / ProcMigration.toName / ProcMigration.toData / ProcMigration.toProc / ProcMigration.alpha_variants_translate_equal / ProcMigration.substProc_captures_the_free_variable"
      note := "The executable model of the reflective calculus carries names explicitly and its substitution erases the binder's own pattern variables before descending. That is correct for shadowing - a variable the receiver itself binds is not substituted inside the body - and it is not correct for capture, because nothing renames the replacement's free variables apart from the binder they are carried under. The defect is exhibited on the smallest example as kernel-checked computation rather than described: two receivers differing only in the name they bind, which no calculus may distinguish, are carried by one substitution to bodies that differ after a single communication delivers a value. A substitution that does this is not a function on the calculus. This is a second, independent instance of the same defect already confirmed in the pattern-level matcher's application of bindings, and the shared cause is a fixed constructor list carrying names, with a hand-written substitution case per constructor. The fragment the model covers is now presented as a binding signature - three sorts, eight term formers, and binding declared in the receiver's continuation rather than managed by hand - and translated into. That is what makes the repair checkable rather than asserted: the two alpha-variants translate to the same term, because a bound occurrence has become a position and there is no name left for a binder to capture, while their images under the model's substitution differ, and differ in exactly the way capture would predict - the free variable the substitution introduced is still used in one translation and has been caught by the receiver's binder in the other. So the model's substitution takes equal inputs to unequal outputs there. Why this row is open: what is landed is the canary and the presentation, not the migration. The representation records bound occurrences as positions. Its defined substitution uses explicit binder-preserving lifts; scope indices alone do not force that choice. Migrating the executable model to that substitution and proving operational correspondence would retire the defect rather than only record it. The blast radius is also unmeasured - capture only bites when open data is substituted, and whether this lane ever does so has not been determined."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "The schema matcher: soundness and recursive-profile completeness"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/BindingSignature.lean: splitVar / splitVar_recombine / instantiate_castTermCtx / bind_liftSub_append / castTermCtx_injective / liftSub_injPrefix / liftSub_weakenVar; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/Strengthening.lean: strengthenT / strengthenA / rename_strengthenT; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/ScopedMatching.lean: recoverBoundVariableBody / recoverBoundVariableBody_eq_some_iff / recoverBoundVariableBody_eq_none_iff / MAcc / smatchAtT / smatchAtA / smatchT / smatchA / MAccLe / MExtends / smatchAtT_mono / smatchAtA_mono / smatchAtT_sound / smatchAtA_sound / MatchingSupportedT / MatchingSupportedA / smatchAtT_complete / smatchAtA_complete / smatchAtT_adequate / smatchAtA_adequate / smatchT_complete / smatchA_complete / smatchT_adequate / smatchA_adequate / smatchA_old_prefix_branch; Mettapedia/GSLT/LanguageDef/ScopedMatcherDependencyBoundary.lean; Mettapedia/GSLT/LanguageDef/ScopedMatchingControls.lean"
      note := "One mutual matcher carries the accumulated bound prefix through rigid operators and nested argument binders. Bound variables match the same position rigidly. Ordinary rule variables receive closed assignments recovered by the original strengthening operation; a lambda may use its own local binder but cannot capture the surrounding prefix. Contextual metavariables use their declared typed dependency context and their actual injective bound-variable argument spine. Projection, recognition and strengthening recover the body. Generic monotonicity and actual-instantiation soundness are proved. Whole-pattern completeness holds on the recursively defined, pattern-only injective-variable profile: an actual instance of a supported pattern is found while retaining the same supplied closing substitution and metavariable assignment. Their equivalence fixes that realizing assignment; it does not assume that unused declarations of uninhabited sorts have total assignments. The original public endpoints specialize this same algorithm to an empty prefix. The old accepted whole-prefix slot retains its exact body, update/check and tail-continuation equation. LanguageDef-derived controls establish nested and repeated-depth supported patterns independently of their targets, invoke the general completeness theorem, and reject accidental capture, conflicting bodies and exchanged same-sort positions. Diagonal or nonvariable metavariable arguments remain outside the profile; an independently instantiable diagonal pattern is still declined, so decline is not generally unsolvability. This is not general higher-order unification, matching modulo equations, inferred permissions or repair of the raw engine. Authored rule elaboration, premise-output scopes and collection-rest execution remain separate open obligations."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "Morphisms of binding signatures: the category, the action on terms, and what travels"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/SignatureMorphism.lean: mapArity / mapArities / mapSorts_id / mapSorts_comp / mapArities_id / mapArity_comp / mapArities_comp / SigMor / SigMor.ident / SigMor.comp / VarMap / mapVar / liftVarMap / mapTerm / mapArgs / SigMor.onTerm / bindArgs_castArgsArity / renameArgs_castArgsArity / countVarArgs_castArgsArity / castArgsArity_trans / castArgsArity_cons / mapTerm_congr / mapArgs_congr / castVarCtx / castVarCtx_zero / castVarCtx_succ / castArgsArity_self / rename_castVarCtx / mapTerm_castVarCtx / mapArgs_castArgsArity / liftVarMap_ident / liftVarMap_comp / mapTerm_ident / mapArgs_ident / mapTerm_comp / mapArgs_comp / liftVarMap_liftRen / liftRen_liftVarMap / mapTerm_rename / mapArgs_rename / rename_mapTerm / renameArgs_mapArgs / liftSub_compat / mapTerm_bind / mapArgs_bind / mapTerm_inst / sameVar_mapVar / liftVarMap_weakenVar / sameVar_lift / countVar_mapTerm / countVarArgs_mapArgs / holeCount_mapTerm / SigMor.onPosition / SigMor.onRewrite / SigMor.onRewrite_carrier / metaInclusion / embed_castTermCtx / mapTerm_metaInclusion / mapArgs_metaInclusion / onTerm_metaInclusion / SortCollapse.OneSrt / SortCollapse.OneOp / SortCollapse.osig / SortCollapse.collapse / SortCollapse.collapsed_lhs / SortCollapse.nameCollapsed / SortCollapse.procCollapsed / SortCollapse.carrier_not_reflected / SortCollapse.transported_contexts_differ / SortCollapse.transported_positions_are_linear / ConstantMerge.TwoOp / ConstantMerge.twoSig / ConstantMerge.OneConst / ConstantMerge.oneSig / ConstantMerge.merge / ConstantMerge.ta / ConstantMerge.tb / ConstantMerge.isA / ConstantMerge.ta_ne_tb / ConstantMerge.onTerm_not_injective"
      note := "A language definition is a triple, and a change of language is a change of its first component, so the construction built over a signature has to travel with it. The morphisms are built here: a map on sorts, a map on operators over the mapped sort, and the requirement that every operator's arity is carried across on the nose, including which sorts each argument binds. This is the strict operator-to-operator case: the selected target operator has exactly the translated argument and binder arities. More general term-valued operator interpretations require their own binding laws; they are not ruled out by this record. In particular, a sequence-sort fold cannot be justified by SigMor alone. The action is indexed by a context translation rather than by an equation between contexts, which limits context-append transports in this action: under an argument binding bs the translated body lives in bs mapped, appended to the translated context, which is exactly where the lifted translation lands, so the equation between the image of an append and the append of the images is never needed. That indexing also identifies two notions that would otherwise be separate - the identity morphism acting along a context translation is renaming, proved, so renaming is what the identity change of signature does rather than a mechanism bolted on beside it. Signatures form a category and terms are a functor on it: identity and composition are built and both laws are proved, the composition law at the term level with no transport at all and at the argument level with one, eliminated by stating the cast-commutation lemmas over variable arity lists where subst discharges them. Renaming and substitution both travel. Substitution travels in the pointwise form - the morphism carries a substitution to any downstream substitution agreeing with it on the translated variables - rather than by pushing the substitution forward, and that is what allows the sort map to be non-injective, since there is then nothing to invert. Plugging travels as a consequence, because plugging is substitution. Occurrence counts travel too, which is what makes a chosen redex position travel: the transported factorisation still plugs and its hole is still used exactly once, so the generator's whole input - rule, both sides, and the occurrence chosen inside the left-hand side - moves, and the carrier of the transported rule is the transported carrier. Adjoining metavariables is itself such a morphism, and the embedding already in use is exactly its action, so the two are one notion rather than two. Two controls say what does not travel backwards. A morphism may collapse sorts: the two positions of one left-hand side whose carriers are different sorts - the obstruction that makes the chosen position extra input - arrive downstream with the same carrier, while remaining two different positions, their one-hole contexts still using different variables and each still using its hole exactly once. So the transport is forward-only and a construction reading the carrier after a collapse cannot recover which occurrence was chosen. And a morphism need not be faithful, exhibited by two distinct constants with one image, so a statement proved downstream is not without further hypotheses a statement about the source."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "Carrying a generated logic along a change of theory: what transports, and the datum the source omits"
      status := .done
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/TheoryMorphism.lean: castTermSort / RewriteMor / RewriteMor.img / RewriteMor.imgCarrier / RewriteMor.imgPred / RewriteMor.rootStep_transport / RewriteMor.poss_transport / RewriteMor.stepsFromPosition_transport / RewriteMor.EnvCovering / RewriteMor.relyPossibly_transport / NoCovering.Srt3 / NoCovering.Op3 / NoCovering.sig3 / NoCovering.OneSrt3 / NoCovering.OneOp3 / NoCovering.osig3 / NoCovering.collapse3 / NoCovering.no_closed_gh / NoCovering.nilO / NoCovering.nilS / NoCovering.SM3 / NoCovering.OM3 / NoCovering.G3 / NoCovering.H3 / NoCovering.lhs3 / NoCovering.ctxt3 / NoCovering.P3 / NoCovering.olhs3 / NoCovering.octxt3 / NoCovering.Q3 / NoCovering.Phi3 / NoCovering.Aup / NoCovering.Adown / NoCovering.Bfalse / NoCovering.t3 / NoCovering.env3 / NoCovering.env3_admissible / NoCovering.gh_not_rely / NoCovering.env3up / NoCovering.source_does_not_hold / NoCovering.target_fails / NoCovering.neither_side_holds / NoCovering.poss_still_transports / Collapsing.K4 / Collapsing.L4 / Collapsing.lhs4 / Collapsing.ctxt4 / Collapsing.P4 / Collapsing.olhs4 / Collapsing.octxt4 / Collapsing.Q4 / Collapsing.pushClose / Collapsing.Phi4 / Collapsing.close0 / Collapsing.I0 / Collapsing.fires / Collapsing.image_fires / Collapsing.poss_here / Collapsing.poss_transported / Collapsing.steps_here / Collapsing.steps_transported / Collapsing.p_is_rely / Collapsing.Aup4 / Collapsing.Adown4 / Collapsing.covering4 / Collapsing.rely_here / Collapsing.rely_transported / Collapsing.aNameO / Collapsing.isAName / Collapsing.isAName_aNameO / Collapsing.image_is_not_aName / Collapsing.not_an_image / Collapsing.freeUp / Collapsing.freeDown / Collapsing.anyTarget / Collapsing.escapingEnv / Collapsing.q_is_rely / Collapsing.closeOf / Collapsing.instOf / Collapsing.free_rely_here / Collapsing.free_target_fails / Collapsing.relyPossibly_does_not_transport / Collapsing.no_env_covering / Collapsing.covering_is_a_datum_not_a_property; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/SignatureMorphism.lean: SigMor.onRewrite; Finding Mind draft 26 section 19.8"
      note := "The source states the construction is functorial and gives the action on a morphism by transport, sending the modality at a chosen position to the modality at the transported position with the transported target predicate, and possibility to possibility of the direct image; morphisms are required to preserve the rewrite relation and the internal-language structure. The syntactic half of that formula is the transport of a one-hole context and its carrier, which is settled by the signature morphisms. This row settles the semantic half, and finds that it splits. A morphism of positioned-rewrite theories is built here as a change of signature, a matching of the rule's sort and of its position's carrier, and a map on rule instances under which both sides and the chosen redex are carried across - which is what preserving the rewrite relation amounts to operationally, since a firing upstream then names a firing downstream with the same decomposition. The existential modalities transport along it. The generated relation travels, possibility travels with the direct image as the source's formula says, and so does the modality at a chosen position in its unindexed form, because both quantifiers there are existential and an instance upstream is already an instance downstream. The rely-indexed modality does not. Its universal quantifier ranges over environments for the rule's variables and therefore points the wrong way through the morphism: a downstream environment has to be pulled back before the upstream specification can be used, and preserving the rewrite relation does not make that possible. The missing datum is isolated as an environment covering - every admissible downstream environment comes from an admissible upstream one, and the instance map keeps the agreement - and transport is proved under it, which is the corrected form of the source's formula for the indexed modality. The index of that universal quantifier is the rule's reliance set and nothing wider, which this row also records as a correction to its own earlier state. An earlier version quantified the modality over closing substitutions of the rule's whole variable context while constraining only the rely variables, and read an obstruction off the resulting vacuity: a sort with no closed terms, sitting at a variable that is neither a rely nor a local parameter, made the upstream specification hold for want of an environment while the collapsed downstream theory had environments and failed. That was an artifact of the index rather than a fact about the theories, and the artifact is now proved to be one. Indexed by the reliance set, no rely environment ever mentions that variable, rely environments exist, and the upstream specification is not vacuous but simply false, since the rule has no instances to witness the existential. Both sides of the former separation are now proved false, so nothing there separated them. The construction is kept with its claim inverted, because the correction is the content. The real obstruction is proved on a theory whose rule fires, and it is a different one: values travel along a change of signature in the forward direction only, while the universal quantifier needs them travelling back. Collapsing sorts creates a closed downstream term at the rely sort which is the image of no closed upstream term of that sort - proved by a head test, since the term type is indexed and its constructors cannot be compared directly - the downstream quantifier ranges over it, and the upstream specification was never asked about it. Upstream the specification holds non-vacuously, with an instance constructed for every rely environment; downstream it fails at the escaping environment; so no covering exists at that typing. The same morphism carries the modality at a typing that pins the value, where the covering is constructed. One morphism, two rely typings, transport at one and not at the other: the covering is a datum a change of theory must supply, not a property it can be asked to have. The existential half is unaffected throughout, and is checked to be, with real inhabitants on both sides."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "The context derivative: one-hole contexts enumerated, with completeness for the binder-free class"
      status := .inProgress
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/PositionEnumeration.lean: deepCount / deepCountArgs / Shallow / deepCount_le / deepCountArgs_le / liftSub_extend_liftRen_succ / bind_rename_liftRen_succ / bindArgs_renameArgs_succ / countVar_rename_liftRen_succ / countVarArgs_renameArgs_succ / ArgsPosition / rootPosition / opPosition / argsHere / argsThere / deriv / derivArgs / deriv_shallow / derivArgs_shallow / sameVar_eq_false_of_countVar_zero / liftSub_inv_of_miss / eq_rename_of_miss / eqArgs_rename_of_miss / hole_inv / rootPosition_mem / mem_deriv / memArgs_deriv / deriv_complete / BinderControl.Srt1 / BinderControl.Op1 / BinderControl.lsig / BinderControl.cst / BinderControl.appcc / BinderControl.deriv_appcc_length / BinderControl.leftPosition / BinderControl.leftPosition_enumerated / BinderControl.lamc / BinderControl.deepCtxt / BinderControl.deepPosition / BinderControl.ctxtIsHole / BinderControl.deepPosition_not_enumerated / BinderControl.deepPosition_not_shallow / BinderControl.deriv_lamc_length; Finding Mind draft 26 chapter 17"
      note := "The generator's first step is to enumerate the chosen subterm occurrences of a left-hand side, and the source asks that the resulting object be the structural derivative of the term rather than a list of syntactic paths. That is what is built here, once, for every signature: the derivative of a term is the list of its one-hole contexts, each carrying the subterm it removed and the proof that plugging it back returns the term. Soundness is by typing rather than by a separate theorem - every entry is a linear redex position of the term it was computed from, because that is the type the enumerator returns - so there is no gap between what the enumerator produces and what a position is. Completeness is proved, and it is the half with content: every shallow linear redex position of a term is one the derivative returns. The proof needs a strengthening lemma that the development did not have - an argument the hole does not occur in is the plugged argument weakened - without which the enumerator output and a given position would be two different terms that happen to plug to the same thing. That lemma is stated once for an arbitrary renaming and substitution inverting each other away from a chosen variable, so the recursion under a binder instantiates it at the lifted pair rather than needing an equation between contexts; stating it over the binder prefix instead would have required the associativity of context extension at every node. Which occurrences are covered is characterised internally rather than described: a one-hole context is a term with a distinguished free variable, so its hole may sit under binders with the hole variable simply shifted, and the number of occurrences sitting under at least one binder is counted by deepCount, with a context shallow when that count is zero. Deep occurrences are proved to be occurrences, which is what makes the name honest. Both directions are exhibited. A term with no binders has all three of its occurrences enumerated, and a position written out by hand at one argument is found by completeness without inspecting the enumeration. A term with a binder has a position that is linear, genuinely decomposes it, and is not returned - and its non-shallowness is read off from completeness rather than computed, which is the sharper statement, since were its hole not under the binder the enumeration would have had to return it. Why this row is open: the class enumerated is the binder-free one. A position whose hole sits under a binder is a legitimate position of this representation - the term plugged into it is scoped outside the binder - and the source requires input-prefix and binder positions as well. Enumerating those needs the hole to be introduced at a depth rather than at the front of the context, which is a further construction and is not built. The abstraction positions, where the redex does use the bound variables, are a different notion already present separately."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "Equations first-class: substitution and plugging descend, and the linearity condition does not"
      status := .inProgress
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/EquationalQuotient.lean: eqClosure_rename / eqArgs_renameArgs / eqClosure_bind / eqArgs_bindArgs / eqClosure_liftSub / eqClosure_bind_pointwise / eqArgs_bindArgs_pointwise / eqClosure_inst / eqSetoid / TermQ / renameQ / bindQ / instQ / bindQ_mk / instQ_mk / StepQ / stepQ_mk / stepQ_congr / Duplication.Srt2 / Duplication.Op2 / Duplication.dsig / Duplication.dupAxiom / Duplication.dupE / Duplication.hole1 / Duplication.hole2 / Duplication.noBody / Duplication.hole1_eq_hole2 / Duplication.holeCount_hole1 / Duplication.holeCount_hole2 / Duplication.holeCount_not_eqClosure_invariant / Duplication.both_factor_equal_terms / Structural.SrtP / Structural.OpP / Structural.psig / Structural.commAxiom / Structural.assocAxiom / Structural.acE / Structural.ax_counts / Structural.countVar_ac / Structural.countVarArgs_ac / Structural.holeCount_ac_invariant"
      note := "The second component of a language definition is not decoration: the objects the semantics talks about are equation classes, not terms, and this row makes that structural on the binding-signature carrier rather than incidental. One thing is discharged by the carrier rather than proved: alpha-conversion is not among the equations, because a bound occurrence is a position, so alpha-equivalent presentations are literally one term and there is nothing for an equation to say about them - which is the layering the goal asks for, obtained by construction. What remains in the component is exactly the structural theory the author writes. Renaming and substitution are proved to descend to the theory, in both senses that matter: equal terms stay equal under a substitution, and equal substitutions send a term to equal terms. The second needs the first at the renaming level, because lifting a substitution under a binder weakens its values. Plugging descends as a consequence, in both arguments at once, so a factorisation is a construction on classes. The quotient carrier is then built and renaming, substitution and plugging are defined on it by descent, so the quotient is again a presheaf on contexts with a substitution action - the second component does not cost the first its structure. Stepping modulo the equations is defined on the quotient by the same descent, which is the precise form of the requirement that the choice of representative cannot alter an observable: the relation is a function of the classes. What is proved not to descend is the interesting half. The number of times a one-hole context uses its hole is not an invariant of the equation class, exhibited on an author's equation that duplicates a variable: the bare hole and its duplicate are one class, one uses its hole once and the other twice, and both are decompositions of terms in one class, so the failure is not an artefact of comparing unrelated things. Since linearity of a context is an occurrence count, the condition that makes a chosen occurrence a redex position is therefore not a property of the class, and the generator's input has to be read off a representative. That is a second sense, independent of the first, in which the position is extra data. A positive control shows the failure is not universal and locates it: under associativity and commutativity - the structural equations a process calculus actually carries - occurrence counts are invariant, proved by induction over the theory with the two axioms discharged by arithmetic, so for those theories linearity does descend. Why this row is open: the requirement covers matching, instruments and formula semantics respecting the equations as well, and those are not touched here; and the general statement behind the positive control - that a theory whose axioms are linear has invariant occurrence counts - is proved for the two-axiom case rather than for linear theories at large."
    }
  , { area := "Syntax"
      title := "The capture defect measured: reachable from the step relation, and its exact safe domain"
      status := .inProgress
      codeRef := "Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/StepRelationCaptureWitness.lean: StepCapture.wrapRule / StepCapture.wrapLang / StepCapture.openTerm / StepCapture.step_result / StepCapture.corrected_result / StepCapture.step_disagrees_with_correction / StepCapture.input_is_open / StepCapture.input_is_scoped_at_one / StepCapture.step_output_is_closed / StepCapture.corrected_output_stays_open / StepCapture.step_does_not_preserve_scope / StepCapture.plain / StepCapture.plainList / StepCapture.plain_of_mem / StepCapture.lifting_eq_applyBindings_of_closed / StepCapture.agreement_at_top_level; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/PatternAsBindingSignature.lean: PatternPresentation.PatSrt / PatternPresentation.PatOp / PatternPresentation.patSig / PatternPresentation.ctxOf / PatternPresentation.ctxOf_add / PatternPresentation.varOfFin / PatternPresentation.finOfVar / PatternPresentation.finOfVar_varOfFin / PatternPresentation.varOfFin_finOfVar / PatternPresentation.lenList / PatternPresentation.toTerm / PatternPresentation.toArgs / PatternPresentation.varIndex / PatternPresentation.varIndex_varOfFin / PatternPresentation.erase / PatternPresentation.eraseArgs / PatternPresentation.erase_castTermCtx / PatternPresentation.erase_toTerm / PatternPresentation.eraseArgs_toArgs / PatternPresentation.varIndex_lt / PatternPresentation.erase_isWellScopedAt / PatternPresentation.eraseArgs_isWellScopedListAt / PatternPresentation.erase_closed / PatternPresentation.ShiftsAt / PatternPresentation.shiftsAt_succ / PatternPresentation.shiftsAt_liftRen / PatternPresentation.liftBVars_liftBVars / PatternPresentation.erase_rename_shift / PatternPresentation.eraseArgs_rename_shift / PatternPresentation.InstAt / PatternPresentation.liftBVars_instantiateBVarAt_bvar / PatternPresentation.instAt_liftSub / PatternPresentation.erase_bind_inst / PatternPresentation.eraseArgs_bind_inst / PatternPresentation.erase_bind_extend; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/PatternRepairWitness.lean: PatternRepair.metas / PatternRepair.schemaSig / PatternRepair.rhsSchema / PatternRepair.bodyX / PatternRepair.bodyFor / PatternRepair.repair_computes_correct / PatternRepair.repair_is_the_only_correct_one / PatternRepair.body_uses_its_scope / PatternRepair.closed_arity_cannot_hold_the_value; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/PatternSubstEquation.lean: PatternSubst.substMetas / PatternSubst.eqSig / PatternSubst.metaB / PatternSubst.metaR / PatternSubst.substLhs / PatternSubst.substRhs / PatternSubst.substAxiom / PatternSubst.patE / PatternSubst.bodyB / PatternSubst.replR / PatternSubst.bodies / PatternSubst.emptySub / PatternSubst.redexTerm / PatternSubst.contractum / PatternSubst.instance_is_the_redex_pair / PatternSubst.subst_evaluates / PatternSubst.erase_redex / PatternSubst.erase_contractum_agrees / PatternSubst.contractum_value / PatternSubst.redex_ne_contractum / PatternSubst.subst_evaluates_everywhere / PatternSubst.argsToSub_single_eq_extend / PatternSubst.erase_contractum_general / PatternSubst.erase_contractum_agrees'; Mettapedia/OSLF/Syntax/SubstitutionRegressionGuard.lean: SubstitutionGuard.etaRule / SubstitutionGuard.etaLang / SubstitutionGuard.redex / SubstitutionGuard.correctBody / SubstitutionGuard.capturedBody / SubstitutionGuard.program / SubstitutionGuard.correctProgram / SubstitutionGuard.capturedProgram / SubstitutionGuard.etaMetas / SubstitutionGuard.etaSchemaSig / SubstitutionGuard.etaRhsSchema / SubstitutionGuard.etaBody / SubstitutionGuard.eta_expansion_is_correct / SubstitutionGuard.current_engine_captures / SubstitutionGuard.captured_ne_correct / SubstitutionGuard.suppliedValue / SubstitutionGuard.correct_uses_its_argument / SubstitutionGuard.captured_ignores_its_argument / SubstitutionGuard.captured_ignores_every_argument / SubstitutionGuard.captured_is_constant_in_its_argument / SubstitutionGuard.correct_is_not_constant / SubstitutionGuard.programs_differ / SubstitutionGuard.both_programs_closed"
      note := "The scoped layer already recorded that the binding applier captures, but a record is not a measurement: it did not say whether anything reaches the defect, what the defect actually is, or what it costs. All three are settled here. Reachability is exhibited on the operation the language-definition layer fires rules with. The live step relation calls the binding applier on a rule's right-hand side, and the five-field core's entry point is definitionally that applier when no reflective presentation is declared. The witness uses only term formers of the pattern language itself - a rule that introduces one abstraction around a matched subterm - and fires on a closed program, so there is nothing undeclared and nothing open at the top. What the defect is, stated correctly: it is not that an open term becomes closed. A control shows that guess is wrong, since a rule may legitimately discard a free variable and such a rule closes an open term without doing anything improper. The breakage is that a retained occurrence changes which binder it refers to. Both reducts are closed, so no ambient-scope check separates them; what separates them is the enclosing binder's own substitution, which reaches the occurrence in the correct reduct and does not reach it in the one the step relation produced, where it has been caught by the binder the rule introduced. The same witness also settles whether the available patch is a repair, and it is not. The lifting applier weakens a matched value by the number of binders it has passed on the right-hand side, which is right only if the value was matched at ambient depth zero; this value was matched one binder deep, so the patch weakens by one too many and produces an index that is not in scope at all, taking a closed program to an open term. So the current operation under-weakens and captures, the patch over-weakens and escapes, and neither computes the reduct. Only a matcher that records the depth at which a value was found can weaken it by the right amount, which is why substituting one applier for the other is not the repair and why the repair has to reach the matcher. The cost is then delimited by a sufficient condition with each of its hypotheses proved necessary. Where every bound value is closed and the pattern uses neither an explicit-substitution node nor a collection rest, the two appliers are proved to be the same function; and for each of those three hypotheses there is a witness satisfying the other two on which they differ, so none can be dropped. The three hypotheses are the three defects: closedness is what the missing weakening would have addressed, the absence of a rest is the splicing gap, and the absence of an explicit substitution is the instantiation gap, since the current operation evaluates such a node while the other preserves it. Nothing already proved over that domain is wrong; the domain is a restriction nobody declared. The replacement carrier is begun alongside: the pattern language presented as a binding signature, with each binder's arity read off the existing instantiation function rather than chosen, including the one that is easy to get wrong, since that function traverses an explicit substitution's body one level deeper than its replacement. Erasure compatibility is proved: translating a scoped pattern into the signature and erasing returns exactly the pattern the existing erasure produces, so the presentation adds structure without changing the term. Well-scopedness preservation is proved too, and proved rather than checked: erasure returns a pattern well-scoped at the length of the context the term was typed in, because the scope is what the type said and erasure only reads positions off. With those in hand the repair is demonstrated on the defect's own rule. The rule's metavariable is adjoined to the signature with the arity of the depth at which it was matched, so its body is a term in a context of that many variables and every occurrence must be applied to arguments naming which variables it may depend on. Instantiating then produces the correct reduct - the one neither existing applier computes - and nothing was told to weaken by any particular amount: the arity said where the value lives and the lifted substitution did the rest. A negative control shows the arity is load-bearing rather than decorative: declared with no arguments, which is what treating a metavariable as an operator constant amounts to, the body type is closed and the value that was matched under a binder is not expressible at all, so the repair is a different type and not a different traversal. The explicit-substitution former is then given its evaluation, as an axiom of the second component rather than by collapsing it into the meta-level substitution, which would change which terms are values and would erase an observation the calculus makes. The axiom needs no machinery beyond the adjoined metavariables: the body is declared with arity one, so an occurrence of it is applied to an argument, and instantiating a metavariable applied to an argument is exactly substituting that argument into its body, so the right-hand side is the body applied to the replacement. It is checked on an instance where the binder bites - the body uses the bound variable under a further binder, so the replacement must be carried past it, with instantiation explicitly lifting substitution under that binder - and the contractum is proved to erase to exactly what the language-definition layer's own binder-eliminating substitution produces from the erased parts. The equation has content: the two sides are different terms, related only by the theory. Nothing further is authored for terms in a context, because the theory is closed under substitution: an instance at the empty context transports to any context by the same descent that makes the quotient a presheaf. A regression guard is added, because a record of what an operation does protects nothing: an implementation can be changed, agree with the record, and still be wrong. The guard states the correct answer positively, on a program whose meaning visibly depends on getting substitution right. Eta-expanding a variable under a binder must give a function that hands its argument to that variable; a capturing substitution gives one that applies its own bound variable to itself, so the identity becomes self-application. The correct answer is proved through the signature, where the metavariable's arity records that the value was matched one binder deep and the schema explicitly supplies the enclosing variable and instantiation performs the corresponding weakening rather than inferring permission from a capture-depth traversal, and it is stated as an equation any implementation must satisfy. That the difference is semantic rather than a matter of indices is proved too: supplying a value for the enclosing binder, the correct reduct hands that value on, while the captured one is proved to be unchanged by every substitution whatsoever, so it is constant in an argument the correct one uses. The translation is then proved to commute with both operations, which upgrades every agreement in this row from an instance to a theorem. Erasure turns the signature's renaming into index shifting and its substitution into the language-definition layer's own binder-eliminating substitution, for every term. Both statements abstract over the map and characterise it by what it does to indices, which is what keeps them free of transports: the recursion under a binder instantiates the characterisation at a higher cutoff instead of needing an equation between contexts. The explicit substitution's evaluation is therefore the existing one always, not on a checked example. Why this row is open: collection-rest splicing and premises are untouched, and the collection case of the applier still inspects the shape of a bound value, which the sequence sort would remove."
    }
